{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V4CEpW2xmQBcNd85BYftgT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"L0 exclusion removal\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"移除 L0 exclusion constraint，仅保留 max_2bit=8，验证 solver 自动发现 L0 sensitivity\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"solver_assigns_8bit_to_L0\": true,\n7\t      \"ppl_without_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n8\t      \"ppl_with_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n9\t      \"delta\": 0.0,\n10\t      \"l0_heads_bit_assignment\": \"8-bit (all 4 L0 heads)\"\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"tables\": [\n13\t      {\n14\t        \"caption\": \"L0 exclusion ablation (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n15\t        \"rows\": [\n16\t          [\n17\t            \"With L0 exclusion\",\n18\t            10.91,\n19\t            \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\",\n20\t            0.25\n21\t          ],\n22\t          [\n23\t            \"Without L0 exclusion\",\n24\t            10.91,\n25\t            \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\",\n26\t            0.25\n27\t          ],\n28\t          [\n29\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n30\t            15.45,\n31\t            \"all 4-bit\",\n32\t            0.25\n33\t          ]\n34\t        ]\n35\t      }\n36\t    ],\n37\t    \"figures\": [],\n38\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 视角：结果 trivially correct，不构成任何贡献。在重构后的论文中仅作为 §3 methodology 的一句话验证（\\\"We verify that the sensitivity-based allocator automatically assigns higher bit-widths to the most sensitive heads without manual exclusion rules\\\"），不列为 finding。\\n\\n\\nSolver 确实自动将 L0 heads 分配到 8-bit——但 reviewer 将此解读为 \\\"profiler works as expected, this is not a finding\\\"。R2 评论：\\\"Of course a sensitivity-based allocator assigns high bits to the most sensitive heads. This is the expected behavior of ANY profiling-based method, not a contribution.\\\" R3 补充：\\\"This just shows the profiler is not broken — it would be alarming if it DIDN'T assign 8-bit to L0.\\\" 在 worst 档下，这个实验从 \\\"solver discovers structure\\\" 的正面叙事 变成 \\\"trivially expected behavior\\\" 的无贡献证据。新 framing 下降级为 methodology validation footnote。\\n\"\n39\t  },\n40\t  {\n41\t    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B full pipeline\",\n42\t    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B (GQA 4:1) 上复制完整 pipeline，测试跨架构泛化\",\n43\t    \"results\": {\n44\t      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 8.09,\n45\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n46\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n47\t      \"delta_vs_uniform\": \"+0.2%\",\n48\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.02,\n49\t      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.07,\n50\t      \"natural_2bit_count\": 2,\n51\t      \"concentration\": 0.57,\n52\t      \"distribution_shape\": \"Spike\"\n53\t    },\n54\t    \"tables\": [\n55\t      {\n56\t        \"caption\": \"Llama-3.1-8B allocation comparison (budget=0.25)\",\n57\t        \"rows\": [\n58\t          [\n59\t            \"BF16 baseline\",\n60\t            8.09,\n61\t            \"—\",\n62\t            \"—\"\n63\t          ],\n64\t          [\n65\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n66\t            8.47,\n67\t            \"all 4-bit\",\n68\t            0.25\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            \"MCKP constrained (k=2)\",\n72\t            8.45,\n73\t            \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n74\t            0.25\n75\t          ],\n76\t          [\n77\t            \"MCKP unconstrained\",\n78\t            8.63,\n79\t            \"{2:12, 4:...}\",\n80\t            0.25\n81\t          ]\n82\t        ]\n83\t      }\n84\t    ],\n85\t    \"figures\": [],\n86\t    \"analysis\": \"在 worst framing 下，Llama 的 negative result 强化 reviewer 论点：per-head allocation 对大多数 架构无价值。但在重构后的 \\\"systematic study\\\" framing 下，Llama 是 boundary condition case (concentration=0.57, just above 0.50 threshold, but t₁/t₅=0.85 violates second criterion)， 证明 diagnostic 的 joint condition 比单一 threshold 更准确。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 仅比 uniform 好 0.02 PPL——reviewer 认为这在 calibration noise 范围内（multi-seed std=0.065 on Qwen，Llama 的 0.02 差距更小）。R1：\\\"A 0.2% improvement is statistically indistinguishable from noise without multi-seed confidence intervals on Llama.\\\" R2 将 1.07× unconstrained degradation 定性为噪声：\\\"1.07× could easily be explained by evaluation variance — you need to show this is significantly different from 1.0.\\\" 在 worst 档下，Llama 成为 \\\"non-uniform allocation is pointless on this architecture\\\" 的直接证据，而 reviewer 进一步推论：\\\"If profiling + MCKP + constraint adds complexity for zero benefit on 7/8 models, the method has negative expected value.\\\" 新 framing 下 Llama 是 \\\"when it doesn't help\\\" 的 case study，支撑 systematic coverage 贡献。\\n\"\n87\t  },\n88\t  {\n89\t    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 full pipeline\",\n90\t    \"description\": \"在 Mistral-7B-v0.3 上复制完整 pipeline\",\n91\t    \"results\": {\n92\t      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 7.035,\n93\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.131,\n94\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.165,\n95\t      \"delta_vs_uniform\": \"-0.4%\",\n96\t      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.034,\n97\t      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.08,\n98\t      \"concentration\": 0.22,\n99\t      \"distribution_shape\": \"Flat\",\n100\t      \"k_ablation_monotonic\": true\n101\t    },\n102\t    \"tables\": [\n103\t      {\n104\t        \"caption\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 k ablation (budget=0.25)\",\n105\t        \"rows\": [\n106\t          [\n107\t            \"k=0 (uniform)\",\n108\t            7.131,\n109\t            0,\n110\t            256,\n111\t            \"optimal\"\n112\t          ],\n113\t          [\n114\t            \"k=4\",\n115\t            7.165,\n116\t            4,\n117\t            252,\n118\t            \"best constrained\"\n119\t          ],\n120\t          [\n121\t            \"k=8\",\n122\t            7.2,\n123\t            8,\n124\t            247,\n125\t            \"\"\n126\t          ],\n127\t          [\n128\t            \"k=16\",\n129\t            7.311,\n130\t            16,\n131\t            238,\n132\t            \"\"\n133\t          ],\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"k=18\",\n136\t            7.323,\n137\t            18,\n138\t            235,\n139\t            \"worst\"\n140\t          ]\n141\t        ]\n142\t      }\n143\t    ],\n144\t    \"figures\": [],\n145\t    \"analysis\": \"Mistral 是 reviewer 攻击 universality claim 的最强武器。Monotonic k-PPL 证明没有任何 k 值能 让 non-uniform 优于 uniform。在重构论文中，Mistral 与 Gemma-2 一起构成 \\\"Flat distribution: skip profiling\\\" 的 taxonomy 类别。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 差 0.034 PPL——non-uniform allocation 在 Mistral 上 actively harmful。 R3 引用此结果：\\\"Your method HURTS performance on Mistral. The profiler reports near-zero sensitivity differences, meaning your entire profiling pipeline produces zero signal on this architecture. This is not 'honest negative result' — it's evidence the method doesn't generalize.\\\" k ablation 单调递增进一步证实：每增加一个 2-bit head 都损害质量，最优 k=0 即 uniform 4-bit。Reviewer 将 1.08× unconstrained 归为 noise，与 Llama 1.07× 一起构成 \\\"mild cases are noise\\\" 的论据。新 framing 下 Mistral 是 \\\"profiler zero-signal\\\" 的典型 case，支撑 \\\"when to skip profiling\\\" 的 diagnostic 贡献。\\n\"\n146\t  },\n147\t  {\n148\t    \"name\": \"Compounding effect sweep\",\n149\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上 sweep max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 compounding threshold\",\n150\t    \"results\": {\n151\t      \"k0_ppl\": 9.81,\n152\t      \"k8_ppl\": 10.05,\n153\t      \"k16_ppl\": 10.42,\n154\t      \"k32_ppl\": 11.6,\n155\t      \"k64_ppl\": 23.22,\n156\t      \"k112_ppl\": \"~98.75\",\n157\t      \"compounding_onset_k\": \"~32\",\n158\t      \"max_compounding_ratio\": 10.07,\n159\t      \"u_shape\": true,\n160\t      \"optimal_k\": 8\n161\t    },\n162\t    \"tables\": [\n163\t      {\n164\t        \"caption\": \"Qwen2.5-7B compounding sweep (budget=0.25, hires profiles)\",\n165\t        \"rows\": [\n166\t          [\n167\t            \"k=0\",\n168\t            9.81,\n169\t            \"baseline (all 4-bit+)\",\n170\t            1.0\n171\t          ],\n172\t          [\n173\t            \"k=8\",\n174\t            10.05,\n175\t            \"constraint threshold\",\n176\t            1.02\n177\t          ],\n178\t          [\n179\t            \"k=16\",\n180\t            10.42,\n181\t            \"\",\n182\t            1.06\n183\t          ],\n184\t          [\n185\t            \"k=32\",\n186\t            11.6,\n187\t            \"onset of rapid degradation\",\n188\t            1.18\n189\t          ],\n190\t          [\n191\t            \"k=64\",\n192\t            23.22,\n193\t            \"catastrophic\",\n194\t            2.37\n195\t          ],\n196\t          [\n197\t            \"k=96\",\n198\t            \"~65\",\n199\t            \"\",\n200\t            \"~6.6\"\n201\t          ],\n202\t          [\n203\t            \"k=112 (unconstrained)\",\n204\t            \"~98.75\",\n205\t            \"\",\n206\t            \"~10.07\"\n207\t          ]\n208\t        ]\n209\t      }\n210\t    ],\n211\t    \"figures\": [],\n212\t    \"analysis\": \"跨架构 compounding sweep 结果实际上 undermines universality：Qwen U-shape (k*=8)，Llama flat-then-cliff (k*=0 即 uniform)，Mistral monotonic (k*=0)。Reviewer 论证：compounding behavior 是架构特异性的，不存在 universal threshold。新 framing 下这成为 taxonomy 的支撑 ——不同 distribution shape 对应不同 compounding pattern。\\n\\n\\nReviewer 承认 PPL 随 k 增加而上升，但拒绝将此称为 \\\"discovery\\\"。R1 引用 RateQuant Appendix M： \\\"Zhang et al. (2024) explicitly discuss that quantization errors compound when multiple heads are simultaneously quantized to low bit-widths. Your sweep merely quantifies a known phenomenon.\\\" R2 补充：\\\"This is the expected behavior of any lossy compression — more aggressive compression leads to more degradation. The curve shape is unsurprising.\\\" R3 指出 U-shape 仅在 Qwen 上出现：\\\"Llama shows flat, Mistral shows monotonic increase. The U-shape is a Qwen-specific artifact, not a universal phenomenon.\\\" 在 worst 档下，compounding sweep 从 \\\"principled motivation for constraint\\\" 降级为 \\\"expected compression behavior on one model\\\"。 新 framing 下放入 §4 \\\"Analysis of allocation failures\\\" 作为 supporting evidence。\\n\"\n213\t  },\n214\t  {\n215\t    \"name\": \"Budget sweep\",\n216\t    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上测试 2×/4×/8× 压缩比下的 constrained MCKP\",\n217\t    \"results\": {\n218\t      \"budget_0.5_mckp_ppl\": \"~9.85\",\n219\t      \"budget_0.5_uniform_ppl\": \"~10.2\",\n220\t      \"budget_0.5_delta\": \"+3.4%\",\n221\t      \"budget_0.25_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n222\t      \"budget_0.25_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n223\t      \"budget_0.25_delta\": \"+29.4%\",\n224\t      \"budget_0.125_mckp_ppl\": \"~57.6\",\n225\t      \"budget_0.125_uniform_2bit_ppl\": \"~2644\",\n226\t      \"budget_0.125_delta\": \">45×\"\n227\t    },\n228\t    \"tables\": [\n229\t      {\n230\t        \"caption\": \"Qwen2.5-7B budget sweep\",\n231\t        \"rows\": [\n232\t          [\n233\t            \"2× (0.50)\",\n234\t            9.85,\n235\t            10.2,\n236\t            \"+3.4%\"\n237\t          ],\n238\t          [\n239\t            \"4× (0.25)\",\n240\t            10.91,\n241\t            15.45,\n242\t            \"+29.4%\"\n243\t          ],\n244\t          [\n245\t            \"8× (0.125)\",\n246\t            57.6,\n247\t            2644,\n248\t            \">45×\"\n249\t          ]\n250\t        ]\n251\t      }\n252\t    ],\n253\t    \"figures\": [],\n254\t    \"analysis\": \"Budget sweep 在新 framing 下成为 \\\"compression ratio analysis\\\" section 的核心——展示 benefit 何时出现、何时消失。但 reviewer 拒绝将 aggressive compression 结果计入贡献 （trivially expected），将 moderate compression 限定为 n=1 evidence。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"The benefit at 2× compression is marginal (3.4%), and 8× compression is unrealistic for deployment — nobody runs 2-bit KV cache in production. The only interesting data point is 4× where you get 29% on ONE model. This is a single-model, single-compression-ratio result dressed up as a general finding.\\\" R1 补充：\\\"At aggressive compression, ANY non-uniform scheme will beat uniform 2-bit — this is trivially true and not a contribution. The interesting regime is moderate compression where your method fails on 7/8 models.\\\" 在 worst 档下，budget sweep 被 reviewer 框定为：mild compression → trivial gain， moderate compression → works on 1/8 only，aggressive compression → trivially expected。\\n\"\n255\t  },\n256\t  {\n257\t    \"name\": \"High-resolution profiling\",\n258\t    \"description\": \"64seq × 2048tok hires profiling on Qwen2.5-7B，测试更精细 profiling 是否改善分配\",\n259\t    \"results\": {\n260\t      \"hires_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n261\t      \"lowres_mckp_ppl\": 11.23,\n262\t      \"improvement_ppl\": 0.32,\n263\t      \"hires_nonzero_2bit\": 100,\n264\t      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit\": 37,\n265\t      \"profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n266\t      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8\n267\t    },\n268\t    \"tables\": [\n269\t      {\n270\t        \"caption\": \"Profiling resolution comparison (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n271\t        \"rows\": [\n272\t          [\n273\t            \"Low-res (16×512)\",\n274\t            11.23,\n275\t            37,\n276\t            \"~5 min\"\n277\t          ],\n278\t          [\n279\t            \"High-res (64×2048)\",\n280\t            10.91,\n281\t            100,\n282\t            \"65.5 min\"\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n286\t            15.45,\n287\t            \"—\",\n288\t            \"0 min\"\n289\t          ]\n290\t        ]\n291\t      }\n292\t    ],\n293\t    \"figures\": [],\n294\t    \"analysis\": \"新 framing 下 profiling resolution 成为 \\\"practitioner guide\\\" 的一部分：低分辨率已足够 判断是否值得 non-uniform (diagnostic)，高分辨率仅在确认 Spread 模型后才值得投入。 但 reviewer 质疑任何 profiling 的 ROI。\\n\\n\\nHires 确实改善了 0.32 PPL（11.23→10.91），但 R3 攻击 profiling cost：\\\"65 minutes of GPU time for 0.32 PPL improvement on a 7B model — at this cost, you could simply run the model in fp16. The profiling overhead negates any memory savings for realistic deployment scenarios.\\\" R1 指出 hires 仅改变了 8/112 heads 的分配：\\\"The low-resolution profile already gets the constraint right (k=8). The hires improvement is marginal fine-tuning within the feasible set, not a qualitative change.\\\" 在 worst 档下，hires profiling 被视为 diminishing returns 的证据——大部分 benefit 来自 constraint（lowres constrained 已优于 uniform）， profiling resolution 是次要因素。\\n\"\n295\t  },\n296\t  {\n297\t    \"name\": \"C4 cross-dataset evaluation\",\n298\t    \"description\": \"用 C4 数据集评估 Qwen2.5-7B，验证结果非 WikiText-2 特异性\",\n299\t    \"results\": {\n300\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n301\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n302\t      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n303\t      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n304\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n305\t      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42\n306\t    },\n307\t    \"tables\": [\n308\t      {\n309\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-dataset calibration (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n310\t        \"rows\": [\n311\t          [\n312\t            \"WTK2-cal → WT2-eval\",\n313\t            10.91,\n314\t            15.45,\n315\t            \"+29.4%\"\n316\t          ],\n317\t          [\n318\t            \"C4-cal → WT2-eval\",\n319\t            11.29,\n320\t            15.45,\n321\t            \"+27.0%\"\n322\t          ],\n323\t          [\n324\t            \"WT2-cal → C4-eval\",\n325\t            20.56,\n326\t            35.42,\n327\t            \"+41.9%\"\n328\t          ],\n329\t          [\n330\t            \"Allocation agreement\",\n331\t            \"96.4%\",\n332\t            \"—\",\n333\t            \"—\"\n334\t          ]\n335\t        ]\n336\t      }\n337\t    ],\n338\t    \"figures\": [],\n339\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-dataset robustness 在新 framing 下是 \\\"benchmark methodology\\\" 贡献的一部分。但 reviewer 认为 96.4% agreement 是 trivially expected，不构成 finding。Llama/Mistral 的 cross-dataset negative results 实际上支撑 \\\"most models don't need profiling\\\" narrative。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Cross-dataset agreement of 96.4% is expected — head sensitivity is a model property, not a data property. This is a sanity check, not a contribution.\\\" R1 关注 cross-domain degradation：\\\"When calibrating on WikiText-2 and evaluating on C4, MCKP PPL is 20.56 vs uniform 35.42 — but both are terrible compared to bf16 baseline of 15.32. The 'benefit' is relative to an already-bad uniform baseline, not absolute quality.\\\" R3：\\\"You only test cross-dataset on Qwen, the one model where your method works. Show me cross-dataset results on Llama and Mistral where the method already fails — does it fail worse?\\\" 实际上 Llama/Mistral cross-dataset 也已测试且确认 negative，但 reviewer 将此视为方法无价值的 更多证据。\\n\"\n340\t  },\n341\t  {\n342\t    \"name\": \"RateQuant greedy comparison\",\n343\t    \"description\": \"实现 RateQuant Algorithm 1 在 {2,4,8,16} 上，展示 greedy 在非连续 bit-width 上失败\",\n344\t    \"results\": {\n345\t      \"ratequant_greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n346\t      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n347\t      \"ratequant_greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n348\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n349\t      \"constrained_delta\": 0.0012\n350\t    },\n351\t    \"tables\": [\n352\t      {\n353\t        \"caption\": \"Solver comparison on {2,4,8,16} (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n354\t        \"rows\": [\n355\t          [\n356\t            \"RateQuant greedy (unconstrained)\",\n357\t            32.45,\n358\t            \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"\n359\t          ],\n360\t          [\n361\t            \"MCKP (unconstrained)\",\n362\t            36.92,\n363\t            \"—\"\n364\t          ],\n365\t          [\n366\t            \"RateQuant greedy + k=8\",\n367\t            11.23,\n368\t            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"MCKP + k=8\",\n372\t            11.23,\n373\t            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n374\t          ],\n375\t          [\n376\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n377\t            15.45,\n378\t            \"all 4-bit\"\n379\t          ]\n380\t        ]\n381\t      }\n382\t    ],\n383\t    \"figures\": [],\n384\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档下最致命的 reviewer objection 之一。RateQuant comparison 需要在论文中 明确 acknowledge：我们不是说 RateQuant 错了，而是说 hardware-aligned bit-width 引入了 RateQuant 未考虑的 failure mode。新 framing 下降级为 \\\"related work comparison\\\" 而非 核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nR1 (最致命攻击)：\\\"RateQuant's greedy is designed for consecutive integers {2,...,6} where Prop. 6 guarantees optimality. You're evaluating it on {2,4,8,16} which violates its assumptions — OF COURSE it fails. This is like criticizing a sorting algorithm for not doing matrix multiplication. RateQuant never claimed to work on non-consecutive sets.\\\" R2：\\\"Both unconstrained solvers fail (greedy 32.45, MCKP 36.92) — this just confirms that the problem is with unconstrained allocation on {2,4,8,16}, which is a known limitation of hardware-aligned bit-widths, not a novel finding.\\\" R3：\\\"Your 'contribution' is adding a single integer parameter k to cap 2-bit heads. This is standard regularization, not a research contribution.\\\" 在 worst 档下，RateQuant comparison 被完全 invalidated：不公平的 comparison + trivial fix = no contribution。\\n\"\n385\t  },\n386\t  {\n387\t    \"name\": \"Oracle comparison\",\n388\t    \"description\": \"Brute-force oracle 在 Qwen2.5-7B 子集上，量化 MCKP 与 oracle 的 gap\",\n389\t    \"results\": {\n390\t      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n391\t      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0183,\n392\t      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0046,\n393\t      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n394\t      \"layers_with_gap\": 3,\n395\t      \"total_evals\": 54\n396\t    },\n397\t    \"tables\": [\n398\t      {\n399\t        \"caption\": \"MCKP vs Oracle (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n400\t        \"rows\": [\n401\t          [\n402\t            \"MCKP\",\n403\t            10.91,\n404\t            \"—\"\n405\t          ],\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"Best oracle gap (L1)\",\n408\t            \"+0.018 PPL\",\n409\t            \"2-bit head swap\"\n410\t          ],\n411\t          [\n412\t            \"Avg oracle gap\",\n413\t            \"+0.005 PPL\",\n414\t            \"—\"\n415\t          ],\n416\t          [\n417\t            \"Layers MCKP=Oracle\",\n418\t            \"5/8\",\n419\t            \"—\"\n420\t          ]\n421\t        ]\n422\t      }\n423\t    ],\n424\t    \"figures\": [],\n425\t    \"analysis\": \"Oracle gap 微小 (0.005 PPL) 在 worst framing 下被解读为 \\\"constrained problem is trivially easy\\\"——任何 solver 都能解决。新 framing 下移入 appendix 作为 methodology validation。\\n\\n\\nR3：\\\"MCKP is near-optimal — but this is EXPECTED given that the cardinality constraint reduces the feasible set to where any reasonable solver works. You showed greedy=MCKP already (plan_016). The oracle comparison just confirms the problem is trivially small under the constraint. This reinforces my view that the constraint is doing all the work, and the solver (including your MCKP formulation) is a non-contribution.\\\" R2：\\\"If the average gap is 0.005 PPL, the solver doesn't matter. You've proven your own contribution irrelevant.\\\" 在 worst 档下，oracle comparison 是 double-edged：证明 MCKP near-optimal BUT ALSO 证明问题在 constraint 下退化到 trivial。\\n\"\n426\t  },\n427\t  {\n428\t    \"name\": \"Cross-domain calibration robustness\",\n429\t    \"description\": \"C4 calibration → WikiText-2 评估（及反向），报告 per-head allocation agreement\",\n430\t    \"results\": {\n431\t      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n432\t      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n433\t      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n434\t      \"cross_domain_delta\": 0.034\n435\t    },\n436\t    \"tables\": [\n437\t      {\n438\t        \"caption\": \"Cross-domain agreement (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n439\t        \"rows\": [\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"WT2↔C4 agreement\",\n442\t            \"96.4%\",\n443\t            \"108/112 heads\"\n444\t          ],\n445\t          [\n446\t            \"PPL gap (C4-cal vs WT2-cal)\",\n447\t            0.034,\n448\t            \"noise range\"\n449\t          ]\n450\t        ]\n451\t      }\n452\t    ],\n453\t    \"figures\": [],\n454\t    \"analysis\": \"Sanity check 级别。在重构论文中仅作为 methodology paragraph 的一句验证，不单列。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"96.4% agreement is a trivial finding. Head sensitivity is a function of model weights, not calibration data — any reasonable calibration set will produce similar profiles. This is a methodology sanity check that belongs in the appendix, not a contribution.\\\" 在 worst 档下， cross-domain robustness 完全不计入贡献。新 framing 下放入 §3 methodology 的 1-2 句话。\\n\"\n455\t  },\n456\t  {\n457\t    \"name\": \"Head sensitivity visualization\",\n458\t    \"description\": \"生成 paper-quality figures: per-head delta heatmap, compounding curve, allocation chart\",\n459\t    \"results\": {\n460\t      \"figures_generated\": 3,\n461\t      \"heatmap_shows_l0_dominance\": true,\n462\t      \"compounding_curve_u_shape\": \"Qwen only\",\n463\t      \"allocation_chart_constraint_effect\": true\n464\t    },\n465\t    \"tables\": [],\n466\t    \"figures\": [],\n467\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 要求更多可视化来支撑 \\\"systematic study\\\" framing。当前 3 张图不够，需扩展到 ~8 张以覆盖所有架构的对比分析。\\n\\n\\nVisualization 本身不被 reviewer 攻击，但 R1 指出：\\\"Your heatmap shows that Layer 0 dominance is the only interesting signal in Qwen's sensitivity profile. This is a single architectural quirk, not a generalizable finding. Show me heatmaps for ALL 8 architectures side by side — that would be a systematic study.\\\" 在 worst 档下，可视化 demand 大幅增加：需要 8 个架构的 对比 heatmap + 3 个架构的 compounding curve + taxonomy 分类图。新 framing 下 visualization 是 \\\"systematic benchmark\\\" 贡献的核心展示方式。\\n\"\n468\t  },\n469\t  {\n470\t    \"name\": \"Downstream task evaluation (Qwen)\",\n471\t    \"description\": \"ARC-C/HellaSwag/PIQA/WinoGrande on Qwen2.5-7B at 4× compression\",\n472\t    \"results\": {\n473\t      \"avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n474\t      \"arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n475\t      \"hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n476\t      \"piqa_delta_pp\": 1.25,\n477\t      \"winogrande_delta_pp\": 1.97,\n478\t      \"arc_c_mckp\": 0.5137,\n479\t      \"arc_c_uniform\": 0.4812,\n480\t      \"arc_c_bf16\": 0.529\n481\t    },\n482\t    \"tables\": [\n483\t      {\n484\t        \"caption\": \"Downstream evaluation across 5 architectures (4×, 0-shot)\",\n485\t        \"rows\": [\n486\t          [\n487\t            \"Qwen (Spread)\",\n488\t            \"+1.9pp avg\",\n489\t            \"+3.16 to +4.00pp range\",\n490\t            \"POSITIVE\"\n491\t          ],\n492\t          [\n493\t            \"Yi (Spike)\",\n494\t            \"-0.77pp avg\",\n495\t            \"-3.24pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n496\t            \"NEGATIVE\"\n497\t          ],\n498\t          [\n499\t            \"Llama (Spike)\",\n500\t            \"-0.99pp avg\",\n501\t            \"-2.65pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n502\t            \"NEGATIVE\"\n503\t          ],\n504\t          [\n505\t            \"Mistral (Flat)\",\n506\t            \"-0.48pp avg\",\n507\t            \"-1.19pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n508\t            \"NEGATIVE\"\n509\t          ],\n510\t          [\n511\t            \"Gemma-2 (Flat)\",\n512\t            \"+0.14pp avg\",\n513\t            \"noise range\",\n514\t            \"NEUTRAL\"\n515\t          ]\n516\t        ]\n517\t      }\n518\t    ],\n519\t    \"figures\": [],\n520\t    \"analysis\": \"跨架构 downstream 数据在 worst 档下是最致命的攻击面。ARC-Challenge 系统性退化 (-3.24pp Yi, -2.65pp Llama, -1.19pp Mistral) 被 reviewer 解读为 \\\"multi-step reasoning tasks are hurt by non-uniform allocation\\\"。新 framing 必须诚实报告这些 negative 结果 并将其作为 \\\"when not to use non-uniform\\\" 的核心 evidence。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Downstream results confirm that your method works on Qwen — we already knew that from PPL. The question is whether it works on OTHER models, and your own downstream results show it HURTS: Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp. Your method has negative expected value across the tested model population.\\\" R3：\\\"72.8% recovery sounds good until you realize it's 72.8% of the gap between uniform 4-bit and bf16 — on a single model. ARC-C shows only +3.16pp which is within single-seed variance range. You provide no confidence intervals for downstream metrics.\\\" R1 最尖锐：\\\"4/4 non-Qwen models show downstream degradation. The paper should be titled 'Non-Uniform KV Cache Quantization Hurts Most Models' Downstream, with Qwen as the Exception.'\\\" 在 worst 档下，downstream eval 成为方法 negative expected value 的 证据。\\n\"\n521\t  },\n522\t  {\n523\t    \"name\": \"70B profiling-only\",\n524\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B profiling only (no full eval)，测试 sensitivity pattern 是否跨 scale\",\n525\t    \"results\": {\n526\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n527\t      \"profiling_completed\": false,\n528\t      \"conclusion\": \"GPU OOM / timeout\"\n529\t    },\n530\t    \"tables\": [],\n531\t    \"figures\": [],\n532\t    \"analysis\": \"Killed 状态在 worst 档下被 reviewer 视为论文的重大 gap。\\\"All results are on 7-14B models — no evidence the method or findings transfer to production-scale models.\\\" 新 framing 必须 在 limitations 明确讨论 scalability。\\n\\n\\nR1：\\\"You claim universality but cannot even run your method on 70B models. The profiling pipeline is too expensive for realistic model sizes. This fundamentally undermines the practical contribution — practitioners work with 70B+ models, not 7B.\\\" R3：\\\"Scalability is the elephant in the room. 65 minutes profiling for 7B × 112 heads — extrapolating to 72B × 1024+ heads means 10+ hours of GPU time, which is unacceptable.\\\" 在 worst 档下， 70B killed 成为 scalability failure 的直接证据。新 framing 需要 acknowledge scalability limitation explicitly 并提出 efficient profiling 作为 future work。\\n\"\n533\t  },\n534\t  {\n535\t    \"name\": \"K/V separation\",\n536\t    \"description\": \"K/V heads 独立 MCKP allocation vs joint K+V\",\n537\t    \"results\": {\n538\t      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n539\t      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n540\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n541\t      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.303,\n542\t      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n543\t      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true\n544\t    },\n545\t    \"tables\": [\n546\t      {\n547\t        \"caption\": \"K/V separation ablation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n548\t        \"rows\": [\n549\t          [\n550\t            \"Joint K+V MCKP\",\n551\t            10.91,\n552\t            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n553\t          ],\n554\t          [\n555\t            \"Separate K/V MCKP\",\n556\t            11.22,\n557\t            \"K:{2:16,...}, V:all-4bit\"\n558\t          ],\n559\t          [\n560\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n561\t            15.45,\n562\t            \"all 4-bit\"\n563\t          ]\n564\t        ]\n565\t      }\n566\t    ],\n567\t    \"figures\": [],\n568\t    \"analysis\": \"Negative result。在新 framing 下报告为 \\\"K/V separation does not improve allocation under our framework\\\"——honest negative finding 支撑 systematic study 的 credibility。\\n\\n\\nR1：\\\"K/V separation HURTS by 0.3 PPL. This means your framework doesn't naturally handle the K/V asymmetry that RateQuant addresses. RateQuant supports asymmetric K/V allocation (K=2.85, V=2.15) which you listed as a differentiation point — but your own experiment shows separation is worse.\\\" R2：\\\"The fact that V heads are all assigned 4-bit under separation suggests V quantization sensitivity is uniform — but you don't analyze WHY, which is the interesting question.\\\" 在 worst 档下，K/V separation negative 被 reviewer 用来论证 framework 不够 flexible，且 RateQuant 在 K/V 处理上更优。\\n\"\n569\t  },\n570\t  {\n571\t    \"name\": \"L0-only heuristic baseline\",\n572\t    \"description\": \"最简 non-uniform 策略：L0 全 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit\",\n573\t    \"results\": {\n574\t      \"status\": \"killed_then_rerun\",\n575\t      \"l0_random_mean_ppl\": 11.69,\n576\t      \"l0_random_median_ppl\": 11.52,\n577\t      \"naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n578\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n579\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n580\t      \"mckp_vs_l0_random_median_gap\": \"-5.2%\"\n581\t    },\n582\t    \"tables\": [\n583\t      {\n584\t        \"caption\": \"L0 heuristic vs MCKP across architectures\",\n585\t        \"rows\": [\n586\t          [\n587\t            \"Qwen — MCKP\",\n588\t            10.91,\n589\t            \"65 min profiling\",\n590\t            \"—\"\n591\t          ],\n592\t          [\n593\t            \"Qwen — L0 heuristic (median)\",\n594\t            11.52,\n595\t            \"0 min\",\n596\t            \"80% of MCKP benefit\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"Qwen — Uniform 4-bit\",\n600\t            15.45,\n601\t            \"0 min\",\n602\t            \"—\"\n603\t          ],\n604\t          [\n605\t            \"Llama — MCKP\",\n606\t            8.45,\n607\t            \"173 min\",\n608\t            \"—\"\n609\t          ],\n610\t          [\n611\t            \"Llama — L0 naive\",\n612\t            8.58,\n613\t            \"0 min\",\n614\t            \"marginal vs MCKP\"\n615\t          ],\n616\t          [\n617\t            \"Mistral — MCKP\",\n618\t            7.16,\n619\t            \"~min\",\n620\t            \"WORSE than uniform\"\n621\t          ]\n622\t        ]\n623\t      }\n624\t    ],\n625\t    \"figures\": [],\n626\t    \"analysis\": \"L0 heuristic 是 worst 档下 reviewer 手中的核武器：simple, zero-cost, gets most of the benefit。新 framing 必须 honest acknowledge 这一点，并将 MCKP 的 marginal benefit (Qwen: 11.52→10.91) 框定为 \\\"the gap that motivates profiling when diagnostic recommends it\\\"。\\n\\n\\nR3 (最致命)：\\\"Your L0 heuristic baseline gets PPL 11.52 (median) vs MCKP 10.91 — a gap of only 0.61 PPL. The L0 heuristic requires ZERO profiling (just assign 8-bit to Layer 0), while MCKP requires 65 minutes of GPU time. The marginal benefit of full profiling + MCKP over the trivial L0 heuristic is minimal. Practitioners should just protect Layer 0 and move on.\\\" R1 补充：\\\"On Llama, MCKP (8.45) barely beats the L0 heuristic (8.58 naive), and on Mistral, MCKP (7.16) is WORSE than uniform (7.13). The sophisticated optimization adds value only on Qwen, and even there the L0 heuristic gets 80% of the benefit for free.\\\" 在 worst 档下，L0 heuristic 被 reviewer 提升为 \\\"the real practical recommendation\\\"—— zero-cost, zero-profiling, captures most of the benefit on the one model where benefit exists。\\n\"\n627\t  },\n628\t  {\n629\t    \"name\": \"Greedy + cardinality constraint ablation\",\n630\t    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy + max_2bit=k=8 vs constrained MCKP\",\n631\t    \"results\": {\n632\t      \"greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.2312,\n633\t      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n634\t      \"delta_vs_mckp\": 0.0012,\n635\t      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n636\t      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n637\t    },\n638\t    \"tables\": [\n639\t      {\n640\t        \"caption\": \"Solver equivalence under constraint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n641\t        \"rows\": [\n642\t          [\n643\t            \"Greedy unconstrained\",\n644\t            32.45,\n645\t            \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"\n646\t          ],\n647\t          [\n648\t            \"MCKP unconstrained\",\n649\t            36.92,\n650\t            \"—\"\n651\t          ],\n652\t          [\n653\t            \"Greedy + k=8\",\n654\t            11.23,\n655\t            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            \"MCKP + k=8\",\n659\t            11.23,\n660\t            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n661\t          ]\n662\t        ]\n663\t      }\n664\t    ],\n665\t    \"figures\": [],\n666\t    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档下 reviewer 最强的 single-line attack：\\\"Your contribution is k=8.\\\" 新 framing 不再将 solver equivalence 作为 surprising finding，而是将其框定为 \\\"the constrained allocation problem is well-behaved\\\" 的方法学观察——支撑 \\\"practitioners need only add one parameter\\\" 的实用结论。\\n\\n\\nR3：\\\"Greedy + constraint = MCKP + constraint (Δ=0.001). This PROVES that MCKP is not a contribution — the constraint alone is sufficient, and any solver (including the simplest greedy) achieves identical results. Your paper presents MCKP as a contribution but your own ablation shows it's irrelevant.\\\" R2：\\\"The solver equivalence is not 'surprising' as you claim — it's the expected consequence of a tight constraint that reduces the feasible set to near-singleton. When max_2bit=8 and budget=0.25, there are very few feasible allocations. Any reasonable solver will find the same one.\\\" R1：\\\"You've demonstrated that your contribution reduces to a single integer hyperparameter k. This is Appendix-level content, not a paper.\\\" 在 worst 档下，solver equivalence 从 \\\"surprising finding that the constraint is the contribution\\\" 翻转为 \\\"proof that there is no contribution beyond a trivial hyperparameter\\\"。\\n\"\n667\t  },\n668\t  {\n669\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed error bars\",\n670\t    \"description\": \"3 个 calibration seed 的 MCKP PPL mean±std (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n671\t    \"results\": {\n672\t      \"mckp_mean\": 10.9878,\n673\t      \"mckp_std\": 0.0648,\n674\t      \"mckp_seeds\": [\n675\t        11.02,\n676\t        10.9,\n677\t        11.05\n678\t      ],\n679\t      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n680\t      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n681\t      \"agreement_pairwise_range\": [\n682\t        0.911,\n683\t        0.946\n684\t      ]\n685\t    },\n686\t    \"tables\": [\n687\t      {\n688\t        \"caption\": \"Multi-seed calibration (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n689\t        \"rows\": [\n690\t          [\n691\t            \"Seed 0\",\n692\t            11.02,\n693\t            \"—\"\n694\t          ],\n695\t          [\n696\t            \"Seed 1\",\n697\t            10.9,\n698\t            \"—\"\n699\t          ],\n700\t          [\n701\t            \"Seed 2\",\n702\t            11.05,\n703\t            \"—\"\n704\t          ],\n705\t          [\n706\t            \"Mean ± std\",\n707\t            \"10.99 ± 0.065\",\n708\t            \"—\"\n709\t          ],\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"Allocation agreement (3-way)\",\n712\t            \"90.2%\",\n713\t            \"—\"\n714\t          ]\n715\t        ]\n716\t      }\n717\t    ],\n718\t    \"figures\": [],\n719\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-seed 在新 framing 下需要扩展：至少 5 seeds on Qwen，3 seeds on 每个额外模型。 10% allocation instability 需要 explicitly discuss 并说明为什么 PPL impact 是 minimal (std=0.065)。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Three seeds is the bare minimum, not rigorous. Standard practice for quantization papers is 5-10 seeds with 95% CI. Your std=0.065 means 95% CI is roughly [10.86, 11.12] — the upper bound is 11.12, still well below uniform 15.45, so the Qwen result holds. But you don't provide multi-seed results for ANY other model. Without error bars on Llama (delta=+0.2%), Yi, Mistral, and Gemma-2, I cannot determine whether their marginal results are signal or noise.\\\" R1：\\\"Allocation agreement of 90.2% across 3 seeds means ~10% of heads are assigned differently depending on calibration data. This instability undermines the profiling-based approach — which 10% of heads get 2-bit vs 4-bit is random.\\\" R3：\\\"The 90% agreement is particularly concerning for deployment: practitioners can't rely on a specific allocation if it changes with calibration data.\\\" 在 worst 档下，multi-seed 结果暴露了两个 weakness：(1) n=3 seeds 不够，(2) allocation instability 10%。\\n\"\n720\t  },\n721\t  {\n722\t    \"name\": \"Runtime/latency benchmark\",\n723\t    \"description\": \"端到端推理延迟和吞吐量测量\",\n724\t    \"results\": {\n725\t      \"bf16_throughput\": 29.6,\n726\t      \"uniform_4bit_throughput\": 23.6,\n727\t      \"mckp_throughput\": 21.8,\n728\t      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n729\t      \"uniform_4bit_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n730\t      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n731\t      \"memory_compression\": \"4× (both uniform and MCKP)\"\n732\t    },\n733\t    \"tables\": [\n734\t      {\n735\t        \"caption\": \"Inference performance (Qwen2.5-7B, single A100)\",\n736\t        \"rows\": [\n737\t          [\n738\t            \"BF16\",\n739\t            29.6,\n740\t            33.78,\n741\t            \"21 MB\"\n742\t          ],\n743\t          [\n744\t            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n745\t            23.6,\n746\t            42.46,\n747\t            \"5.25 MB\"\n748\t          ],\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"MCKP (k=8)\",\n751\t            21.8,\n752\t            46.09,\n753\t            \"5.25 MB\"\n754\t          ],\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"MCKP overhead vs uniform\",\n757\t            \"-7.6%\",\n758\t            \"+8.5%\",\n759\t            \"0%\"\n760\t          ]\n761\t        ]\n762\t      }\n763\t    ],\n764\t    \"figures\": [],\n765\t    \"analysis\": \"Runtime overhead 是新 framing 下必须直面的 weakness。MCKP 同压缩比下比 uniform 慢 8%， 这意味着 Qwen 的 +29% PPL improvement 伴随 8% latency cost。新 framing 应承认这一 tradeoff 并将 kernel optimization 列为 future work。对 7/8 无 PPL benefit 的模型， mixed-precision 的 latency overhead 是 pure cost——进一步支撑 \\\"use diagnostic before profiling\\\" 的实用建议。\\n\\nR1 (最致命)：\\\"Mixed-precision MCKP is SLOWER than uniform 4-bit: 21.8 tok/s vs 23.6 tok/s (8% throughput loss), 46.1 ms vs 42.5 ms decode latency (8.5% overhead). You achieve the SAME memory compression (4×) with WORSE latency. For 7/8 models where MCKP doesn't improve PPL, this is a pure loss — worse latency for no quality benefit. Even on Qwen where PPL improves, practitioners must decide whether +29% PPL improvement justifies -8% throughput.\\\" R2：\\\"The uniform 4-bit itself is already 20% slower than bf16 — your method adds another 8% on top. The memory savings don't translate to speed because your mixed-precision dequantization kernel is not optimized.\\\" R3：\\\"The 0.005s solver time is irrelevant — the problem is inference-time overhead from heterogeneous bit-width lookup, which you don't address.\\\" 在 worst 档下，runtime 结果是 practical deployment value claim 的致命打击。\\n\"\n766\t  }\n767\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6af5c089-c8bd-4731-91a8-bdbf5ff728e6","uuid":"fa2a09b4-364f-4c2e-b5e8-29328042e721","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:41:31.373Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021448/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0 exclusion removal\",\n    \"description\": \"移除 L0 exclusion constraint，仅保留 max_2bit=8，验证 solver 自动发现 L0 sensitivity\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"solver_assigns_8bit_to_L0\": true,\n      \"ppl_without_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n      \"ppl_with_l0_exclusion\": 10.91,\n      \"delta\": 0.0,\n      \"l0_heads_bit_assignment\": \"8-bit (all 4 L0 heads)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"L0 exclusion ablation (Qwen2.5-7B, budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"With L0 exclusion\",\n            10.91,\n            \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\",\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Without L0 exclusion\",\n            10.91,\n            \"{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}\",\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            \"all 4-bit\",\n            0.25\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 视角：结果 trivially correct，不构成任何贡献。在重构后的论文中仅作为 §3 methodology 的一句话验证（\\\"We verify that the sensitivity-based allocator automatically assigns higher bit-widths to the most sensitive heads without manual exclusion rules\\\"），不列为 finding。\\n\\n\\nSolver 确实自动将 L0 heads 分配到 8-bit——但 reviewer 将此解读为 \\\"profiler works as expected, this is not a finding\\\"。R2 评论：\\\"Of course a sensitivity-based allocator assigns high bits to the most sensitive heads. This is the expected behavior of ANY profiling-based method, not a contribution.\\\" R3 补充：\\\"This just shows the profiler is not broken — it would be alarming if it DIDN'T assign 8-bit to L0.\\\" 在 worst 档下，这个实验从 \\\"solver discovers structure\\\" 的正面叙事 变成 \\\"trivially expected behavior\\\" 的无贡献证据。新 framing 下降级为 methodology validation footnote。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama-3.1-8B full pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Llama-3.1-8B (GQA 4:1) 上复制完整 pipeline，测试跨架构泛化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 8.09,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 8.47,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 8.45,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform\": \"+0.2%\",\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.02,\n      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.07,\n      \"natural_2bit_count\": 2,\n      \"concentration\": 0.57,\n      \"distribution_shape\": \"Spike\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Llama-3.1-8B allocation comparison (budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BF16 baseline\",\n            8.09,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            8.47,\n            \"all 4-bit\",\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP constrained (k=2)\",\n            8.45,\n            \"{2:2, 4:253, 8:1}\",\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP unconstrained\",\n            8.63,\n            \"{2:12, 4:...}\",\n            0.25\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在 worst framing 下，Llama 的 negative result 强化 reviewer 论点：per-head allocation 对大多数 架构无价值。但在重构后的 \\\"systematic study\\\" framing 下，Llama 是 boundary condition case (concentration=0.57, just above 0.50 threshold, but t₁/t₅=0.85 violates second criterion)， 证明 diagnostic 的 joint condition 比单一 threshold 更准确。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 仅比 uniform 好 0.02 PPL——reviewer 认为这在 calibration noise 范围内（multi-seed std=0.065 on Qwen，Llama 的 0.02 差距更小）。R1：\\\"A 0.2% improvement is statistically indistinguishable from noise without multi-seed confidence intervals on Llama.\\\" R2 将 1.07× unconstrained degradation 定性为噪声：\\\"1.07× could easily be explained by evaluation variance — you need to show this is significantly different from 1.0.\\\" 在 worst 档下，Llama 成为 \\\"non-uniform allocation is pointless on this architecture\\\" 的直接证据，而 reviewer 进一步推论：\\\"If profiling + MCKP + constraint adds complexity for zero benefit on 7/8 models, the method has negative expected value.\\\" 新 framing 下 Llama 是 \\\"when it doesn't help\\\" 的 case study，支撑 systematic coverage 贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 full pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Mistral-7B-v0.3 上复制完整 pipeline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_ppl_bf16\": 7.035,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 7.131,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 7.165,\n      \"delta_vs_uniform\": \"-0.4%\",\n      \"delta_vs_uniform_ppl\": -0.034,\n      \"unconstrained_degradation_ratio\": 1.08,\n      \"concentration\": 0.22,\n      \"distribution_shape\": \"Flat\",\n      \"k_ablation_monotonic\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Mistral-7B-v0.3 k ablation (budget=0.25)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"k=0 (uniform)\",\n            7.131,\n            0,\n            256,\n            \"optimal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=4\",\n            7.165,\n            4,\n            252,\n            \"best constrained\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=8\",\n            7.2,\n            8,\n            247,\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=16\",\n            7.311,\n            16,\n            238,\n            \"\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=18\",\n            7.323,\n            18,\n            235,\n            \"worst\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Mistral 是 reviewer 攻击 universality claim 的最强武器。Monotonic k-PPL 证明没有任何 k 值能 让 non-uniform 优于 uniform。在重构论文中，Mistral 与 Gemma-2 一起构成 \\\"Flat distribution: skip profiling\\\" 的 taxonomy 类别。\\n\\n\\nMCKP 比 uniform 4-bit 差 0.034 PPL——non-uniform allocation 在 Mistral 上 actively harmful。 R3 引用此结果：\\\"Your method HURTS performance on Mistral. The profiler reports near-zero sensitivity differences, meaning your entire profiling pipeline produces zero signal on this architecture. This is not 'honest negative result' — it's evidence the method doesn't generalize.\\\" k ablation 单调递增进一步证实：每增加一个 2-bit head 都损害质量，最优 k=0 即 uniform 4-bit。Reviewer 将 1.08× unconstrained 归为 noise，与 Llama 1.07× 一起构成 \\\"mild cases are noise\\\" 的论据。新 framing 下 Mistral 是 \\\"profiler zero-signal\\\" 的典型 case，支撑 \\\"when to skip profiling\\\" 的 diagnostic 贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Compounding effect sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上 sweep max_2bit 从 0 到 112，绘制 compounding threshold\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"k0_ppl\": 9.81,\n      \"k8_ppl\": 10.05,\n      \"k16_ppl\": 10.42,\n      \"k32_ppl\": 11.6,\n      \"k64_ppl\": 23.22,\n      \"k112_ppl\": \"~98.75\",\n      \"compounding_onset_k\": \"~32\",\n      \"max_compounding_ratio\": 10.07,\n      \"u_shape\": true,\n      \"optimal_k\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Qwen2.5-7B compounding sweep (budget=0.25, hires profiles)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"k=0\",\n            9.81,\n            \"baseline (all 4-bit+)\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=8\",\n            10.05,\n            \"constraint threshold\",\n            1.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=16\",\n            10.42,\n            \"\",\n            1.06\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=32\",\n            11.6,\n            \"onset of rapid degradation\",\n            1.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=64\",\n            23.22,\n            \"catastrophic\",\n            2.37\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=96\",\n            \"~65\",\n            \"\",\n            \"~6.6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"k=112 (unconstrained)\",\n            \"~98.75\",\n            \"\",\n            \"~10.07\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"跨架构 compounding sweep 结果实际上 undermines universality：Qwen U-shape (k*=8)，Llama flat-then-cliff (k*=0 即 uniform)，Mistral monotonic (k*=0)。Reviewer 论证：compounding behavior 是架构特异性的，不存在 universal threshold。新 framing 下这成为 taxonomy 的支撑 ——不同 distribution shape 对应不同 compounding pattern。\\n\\n\\nReviewer 承认 PPL 随 k 增加而上升，但拒绝将此称为 \\\"discovery\\\"。R1 引用 RateQuant Appendix M： \\\"Zhang et al. (2024) explicitly discuss that quantization errors compound when multiple heads are simultaneously quantized to low bit-widths. Your sweep merely quantifies a known phenomenon.\\\" R2 补充：\\\"This is the expected behavior of any lossy compression — more aggressive compression leads to more degradation. The curve shape is unsurprising.\\\" R3 指出 U-shape 仅在 Qwen 上出现：\\\"Llama shows flat, Mistral shows monotonic increase. The U-shape is a Qwen-specific artifact, not a universal phenomenon.\\\" 在 worst 档下，compounding sweep 从 \\\"principled motivation for constraint\\\" 降级为 \\\"expected compression behavior on one model\\\"。 新 framing 下放入 §4 \\\"Analysis of allocation failures\\\" 作为 supporting evidence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Budget sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Qwen2.5-7B 上测试 2×/4×/8× 压缩比下的 constrained MCKP\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"budget_0.5_mckp_ppl\": \"~9.85\",\n      \"budget_0.5_uniform_ppl\": \"~10.2\",\n      \"budget_0.5_delta\": \"+3.4%\",\n      \"budget_0.25_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"budget_0.25_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"budget_0.25_delta\": \"+29.4%\",\n      \"budget_0.125_mckp_ppl\": \"~57.6\",\n      \"budget_0.125_uniform_2bit_ppl\": \"~2644\",\n      \"budget_0.125_delta\": \">45×\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Qwen2.5-7B budget sweep\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"2× (0.50)\",\n            9.85,\n            10.2,\n            \"+3.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4× (0.25)\",\n            10.91,\n            15.45,\n            \"+29.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"8× (0.125)\",\n            57.6,\n            2644,\n            \">45×\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Budget sweep 在新 framing 下成为 \\\"compression ratio analysis\\\" section 的核心——展示 benefit 何时出现、何时消失。但 reviewer 拒绝将 aggressive compression 结果计入贡献 （trivially expected），将 moderate compression 限定为 n=1 evidence。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"The benefit at 2× compression is marginal (3.4%), and 8× compression is unrealistic for deployment — nobody runs 2-bit KV cache in production. The only interesting data point is 4× where you get 29% on ONE model. This is a single-model, single-compression-ratio result dressed up as a general finding.\\\" R1 补充：\\\"At aggressive compression, ANY non-uniform scheme will beat uniform 2-bit — this is trivially true and not a contribution. The interesting regime is moderate compression where your method fails on 7/8 models.\\\" 在 worst 档下，budget sweep 被 reviewer 框定为：mild compression → trivial gain， moderate compression → works on 1/8 only，aggressive compression → trivially expected。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"High-resolution profiling\",\n    \"description\": \"64seq × 2048tok hires profiling on Qwen2.5-7B，测试更精细 profiling 是否改善分配\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hires_mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"lowres_mckp_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"improvement_ppl\": 0.32,\n      \"hires_nonzero_2bit\": 100,\n      \"lowres_nonzero_2bit\": 37,\n      \"profiling_time_min\": 65.5,\n      \"allocation_diff_count\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Profiling resolution comparison (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Low-res (16×512)\",\n            11.23,\n            37,\n            \"~5 min\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"High-res (64×2048)\",\n            10.91,\n            100,\n            \"65.5 min\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            \"—\",\n            \"0 min\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"新 framing 下 profiling resolution 成为 \\\"practitioner guide\\\" 的一部分：低分辨率已足够 判断是否值得 non-uniform (diagnostic)，高分辨率仅在确认 Spread 模型后才值得投入。 但 reviewer 质疑任何 profiling 的 ROI。\\n\\n\\nHires 确实改善了 0.32 PPL（11.23→10.91），但 R3 攻击 profiling cost：\\\"65 minutes of GPU time for 0.32 PPL improvement on a 7B model — at this cost, you could simply run the model in fp16. The profiling overhead negates any memory savings for realistic deployment scenarios.\\\" R1 指出 hires 仅改变了 8/112 heads 的分配：\\\"The low-resolution profile already gets the constraint right (k=8). The hires improvement is marginal fine-tuning within the feasible set, not a qualitative change.\\\" 在 worst 档下，hires profiling 被视为 diminishing returns 的证据——大部分 benefit 来自 constraint（lowres constrained 已优于 uniform）， profiling resolution 是次要因素。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"C4 cross-dataset evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"用 C4 数据集评估 Qwen2.5-7B，验证结果非 WikiText-2 特异性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_uniform_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_mckp_ppl\": 20.56,\n      \"cross_domain_wt2_to_c4_uniform_ppl\": 35.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-dataset calibration (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"WTK2-cal → WT2-eval\",\n            10.91,\n            15.45,\n            \"+29.4%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4-cal → WT2-eval\",\n            11.29,\n            15.45,\n            \"+27.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WT2-cal → C4-eval\",\n            20.56,\n            35.42,\n            \"+41.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Allocation agreement\",\n            \"96.4%\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-dataset robustness 在新 framing 下是 \\\"benchmark methodology\\\" 贡献的一部分。但 reviewer 认为 96.4% agreement 是 trivially expected，不构成 finding。Llama/Mistral 的 cross-dataset negative results 实际上支撑 \\\"most models don't need profiling\\\" narrative。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Cross-dataset agreement of 96.4% is expected — head sensitivity is a model property, not a data property. This is a sanity check, not a contribution.\\\" R1 关注 cross-domain degradation：\\\"When calibrating on WikiText-2 and evaluating on C4, MCKP PPL is 20.56 vs uniform 35.42 — but both are terrible compared to bf16 baseline of 15.32. The 'benefit' is relative to an already-bad uniform baseline, not absolute quality.\\\" R3：\\\"You only test cross-dataset on Qwen, the one model where your method works. Show me cross-dataset results on Llama and Mistral where the method already fails — does it fail worse?\\\" 实际上 Llama/Mistral cross-dataset 也已测试且确认 negative，但 reviewer 将此视为方法无价值的 更多证据。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RateQuant greedy comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 RateQuant Algorithm 1 在 {2,4,8,16} 上，展示 greedy 在非连续 bit-width 上失败\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ratequant_greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"mckp_unconstrained_ppl\": 36.92,\n      \"ratequant_greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"constrained_delta\": 0.0012\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Solver comparison on {2,4,8,16} (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RateQuant greedy (unconstrained)\",\n            32.45,\n            \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP (unconstrained)\",\n            36.92,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RateQuant greedy + k=8\",\n            11.23,\n            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP + k=8\",\n            11.23,\n            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            \"all 4-bit\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档下最致命的 reviewer objection 之一。RateQuant comparison 需要在论文中 明确 acknowledge：我们不是说 RateQuant 错了，而是说 hardware-aligned bit-width 引入了 RateQuant 未考虑的 failure mode。新 framing 下降级为 \\\"related work comparison\\\" 而非 核心贡献。\\n\\n\\nR1 (最致命攻击)：\\\"RateQuant's greedy is designed for consecutive integers {2,...,6} where Prop. 6 guarantees optimality. You're evaluating it on {2,4,8,16} which violates its assumptions — OF COURSE it fails. This is like criticizing a sorting algorithm for not doing matrix multiplication. RateQuant never claimed to work on non-consecutive sets.\\\" R2：\\\"Both unconstrained solvers fail (greedy 32.45, MCKP 36.92) — this just confirms that the problem is with unconstrained allocation on {2,4,8,16}, which is a known limitation of hardware-aligned bit-widths, not a novel finding.\\\" R3：\\\"Your 'contribution' is adding a single integer parameter k to cap 2-bit heads. This is standard regularization, not a research contribution.\\\" 在 worst 档下，RateQuant comparison 被完全 invalidated：不公平的 comparison + trivial fix = no contribution。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Oracle comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Brute-force oracle 在 Qwen2.5-7B 子集上，量化 MCKP 与 oracle 的 gap\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"max_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0183,\n      \"avg_oracle_gap_ppl\": 0.0046,\n      \"layers_mckp_optimal\": \"5/8\",\n      \"layers_with_gap\": 3,\n      \"total_evals\": 54\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"MCKP vs Oracle (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MCKP\",\n            10.91,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Best oracle gap (L1)\",\n            \"+0.018 PPL\",\n            \"2-bit head swap\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Avg oracle gap\",\n            \"+0.005 PPL\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Layers MCKP=Oracle\",\n            \"5/8\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Oracle gap 微小 (0.005 PPL) 在 worst framing 下被解读为 \\\"constrained problem is trivially easy\\\"——任何 solver 都能解决。新 framing 下移入 appendix 作为 methodology validation。\\n\\n\\nR3：\\\"MCKP is near-optimal — but this is EXPECTED given that the cardinality constraint reduces the feasible set to where any reasonable solver works. You showed greedy=MCKP already (plan_016). The oracle comparison just confirms the problem is trivially small under the constraint. This reinforces my view that the constraint is doing all the work, and the solver (including your MCKP formulation) is a non-contribution.\\\" R2：\\\"If the average gap is 0.005 PPL, the solver doesn't matter. You've proven your own contribution irrelevant.\\\" 在 worst 档下，oracle comparison 是 double-edged：证明 MCKP near-optimal BUT ALSO 证明问题在 constraint 下退化到 trivial。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-domain calibration robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"C4 calibration → WikiText-2 评估（及反向），报告 per-head allocation agreement\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"allocation_agreement_c4_vs_wt2\": 0.964,\n      \"agreement_heads\": \"108/112\",\n      \"c4_cal_wt2_eval_mckp_ppl\": 11.29,\n      \"cross_domain_delta\": 0.034\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Cross-domain agreement (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"WT2↔C4 agreement\",\n            \"96.4%\",\n            \"108/112 heads\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"PPL gap (C4-cal vs WT2-cal)\",\n            0.034,\n            \"noise range\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Sanity check 级别。在重构论文中仅作为 methodology paragraph 的一句验证，不单列。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"96.4% agreement is a trivial finding. Head sensitivity is a function of model weights, not calibration data — any reasonable calibration set will produce similar profiles. This is a methodology sanity check that belongs in the appendix, not a contribution.\\\" 在 worst 档下， cross-domain robustness 完全不计入贡献。新 framing 下放入 §3 methodology 的 1-2 句话。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Head sensitivity visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"生成 paper-quality figures: per-head delta heatmap, compounding curve, allocation chart\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"figures_generated\": 3,\n      \"heatmap_shows_l0_dominance\": true,\n      \"compounding_curve_u_shape\": \"Qwen only\",\n      \"allocation_chart_constraint_effect\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 要求更多可视化来支撑 \\\"systematic study\\\" framing。当前 3 张图不够，需扩展到 ~8 张以覆盖所有架构的对比分析。\\n\\n\\nVisualization 本身不被 reviewer 攻击，但 R1 指出：\\\"Your heatmap shows that Layer 0 dominance is the only interesting signal in Qwen's sensitivity profile. This is a single architectural quirk, not a generalizable finding. Show me heatmaps for ALL 8 architectures side by side — that would be a systematic study.\\\" 在 worst 档下，可视化 demand 大幅增加：需要 8 个架构的 对比 heatmap + 3 个架构的 compounding curve + taxonomy 分类图。新 framing 下 visualization 是 \\\"systematic benchmark\\\" 贡献的核心展示方式。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Downstream task evaluation (Qwen)\",\n    \"description\": \"ARC-C/HellaSwag/PIQA/WinoGrande on Qwen2.5-7B at 4× compression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"avg_recovery\": 0.728,\n      \"arc_c_delta_pp\": 3.16,\n      \"hellaswag_delta_pp\": 4.0,\n      \"piqa_delta_pp\": 1.25,\n      \"winogrande_delta_pp\": 1.97,\n      \"arc_c_mckp\": 0.5137,\n      \"arc_c_uniform\": 0.4812,\n      \"arc_c_bf16\": 0.529\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Downstream evaluation across 5 architectures (4×, 0-shot)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen (Spread)\",\n            \"+1.9pp avg\",\n            \"+3.16 to +4.00pp range\",\n            \"POSITIVE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Yi (Spike)\",\n            \"-0.77pp avg\",\n            \"-3.24pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n            \"NEGATIVE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama (Spike)\",\n            \"-0.99pp avg\",\n            \"-2.65pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n            \"NEGATIVE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral (Flat)\",\n            \"-0.48pp avg\",\n            \"-1.19pp worst (ARC-C)\",\n            \"NEGATIVE\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-2 (Flat)\",\n            \"+0.14pp avg\",\n            \"noise range\",\n            \"NEUTRAL\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"跨架构 downstream 数据在 worst 档下是最致命的攻击面。ARC-Challenge 系统性退化 (-3.24pp Yi, -2.65pp Llama, -1.19pp Mistral) 被 reviewer 解读为 \\\"multi-step reasoning tasks are hurt by non-uniform allocation\\\"。新 framing 必须诚实报告这些 negative 结果 并将其作为 \\\"when not to use non-uniform\\\" 的核心 evidence。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Downstream results confirm that your method works on Qwen — we already knew that from PPL. The question is whether it works on OTHER models, and your own downstream results show it HURTS: Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp. Your method has negative expected value across the tested model population.\\\" R3：\\\"72.8% recovery sounds good until you realize it's 72.8% of the gap between uniform 4-bit and bf16 — on a single model. ARC-C shows only +3.16pp which is within single-seed variance range. You provide no confidence intervals for downstream metrics.\\\" R1 最尖锐：\\\"4/4 non-Qwen models show downstream degradation. The paper should be titled 'Non-Uniform KV Cache Quantization Hurts Most Models' Downstream, with Qwen as the Exception.'\\\" 在 worst 档下，downstream eval 成为方法 negative expected value 的 证据。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"70B profiling-only\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B profiling only (no full eval)，测试 sensitivity pattern 是否跨 scale\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"profiling_completed\": false,\n      \"conclusion\": \"GPU OOM / timeout\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Killed 状态在 worst 档下被 reviewer 视为论文的重大 gap。\\\"All results are on 7-14B models — no evidence the method or findings transfer to production-scale models.\\\" 新 framing 必须 在 limitations 明确讨论 scalability。\\n\\n\\nR1：\\\"You claim universality but cannot even run your method on 70B models. The profiling pipeline is too expensive for realistic model sizes. This fundamentally undermines the practical contribution — practitioners work with 70B+ models, not 7B.\\\" R3：\\\"Scalability is the elephant in the room. 65 minutes profiling for 7B × 112 heads — extrapolating to 72B × 1024+ heads means 10+ hours of GPU time, which is unacceptable.\\\" 在 worst 档下， 70B killed 成为 scalability failure 的直接证据。新 framing 需要 acknowledge scalability limitation explicitly 并提出 efficient profiling 作为 future work。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"K/V separation\",\n    \"description\": \"K/V heads 独立 MCKP allocation vs joint K+V\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"kv_sep_ppl\": 11.22,\n      \"joint_kv_ppl\": 10.91,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"delta_sep_vs_joint\": 0.303,\n      \"sep_k_2bit_count\": 16,\n      \"sep_v_uniform_4bit\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"K/V separation ablation (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Joint K+V MCKP\",\n            10.91,\n            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Separate K/V MCKP\",\n            11.22,\n            \"K:{2:16,...}, V:all-4bit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            \"all 4-bit\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Negative result。在新 framing 下报告为 \\\"K/V separation does not improve allocation under our framework\\\"——honest negative finding 支撑 systematic study 的 credibility。\\n\\n\\nR1：\\\"K/V separation HURTS by 0.3 PPL. This means your framework doesn't naturally handle the K/V asymmetry that RateQuant addresses. RateQuant supports asymmetric K/V allocation (K=2.85, V=2.15) which you listed as a differentiation point — but your own experiment shows separation is worse.\\\" R2：\\\"The fact that V heads are all assigned 4-bit under separation suggests V quantization sensitivity is uniform — but you don't analyze WHY, which is the interesting question.\\\" 在 worst 档下，K/V separation negative 被 reviewer 用来论证 framework 不够 flexible，且 RateQuant 在 K/V 处理上更优。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"L0-only heuristic baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"最简 non-uniform 策略：L0 全 8-bit，其余 uniform 4-bit\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed_then_rerun\",\n      \"l0_random_mean_ppl\": 11.69,\n      \"l0_random_median_ppl\": 11.52,\n      \"naive_positional_ppl\": 12.23,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"mckp_vs_l0_random_median_gap\": \"-5.2%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"L0 heuristic vs MCKP across architectures\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen — MCKP\",\n            10.91,\n            \"65 min profiling\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen — L0 heuristic (median)\",\n            11.52,\n            \"0 min\",\n            \"80% of MCKP benefit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen — Uniform 4-bit\",\n            15.45,\n            \"0 min\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama — MCKP\",\n            8.45,\n            \"173 min\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama — L0 naive\",\n            8.58,\n            \"0 min\",\n            \"marginal vs MCKP\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral — MCKP\",\n            7.16,\n            \"~min\",\n            \"WORSE than uniform\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"L0 heuristic 是 worst 档下 reviewer 手中的核武器：simple, zero-cost, gets most of the benefit。新 framing 必须 honest acknowledge 这一点，并将 MCKP 的 marginal benefit (Qwen: 11.52→10.91) 框定为 \\\"the gap that motivates profiling when diagnostic recommends it\\\"。\\n\\n\\nR3 (最致命)：\\\"Your L0 heuristic baseline gets PPL 11.52 (median) vs MCKP 10.91 — a gap of only 0.61 PPL. The L0 heuristic requires ZERO profiling (just assign 8-bit to Layer 0), while MCKP requires 65 minutes of GPU time. The marginal benefit of full profiling + MCKP over the trivial L0 heuristic is minimal. Practitioners should just protect Layer 0 and move on.\\\" R1 补充：\\\"On Llama, MCKP (8.45) barely beats the L0 heuristic (8.58 naive), and on Mistral, MCKP (7.16) is WORSE than uniform (7.13). The sophisticated optimization adds value only on Qwen, and even there the L0 heuristic gets 80% of the benefit for free.\\\" 在 worst 档下，L0 heuristic 被 reviewer 提升为 \\\"the real practical recommendation\\\"—— zero-cost, zero-profiling, captures most of the benefit on the one model where benefit exists。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Greedy + cardinality constraint ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RateQuant greedy + max_2bit=k=8 vs constrained MCKP\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"greedy_constrained_ppl\": 11.2312,\n      \"mckp_constrained_ppl\": 11.23,\n      \"delta_vs_mckp\": 0.0012,\n      \"greedy_unconstrained_ppl\": 32.45,\n      \"bit_distribution\": \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Solver equivalence under constraint (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Greedy unconstrained\",\n            32.45,\n            \"{2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP unconstrained\",\n            36.92,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Greedy + k=8\",\n            11.23,\n            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP + k=8\",\n            11.23,\n            \"{2:8, 4:100, 8:4}\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是 worst 档下 reviewer 最强的 single-line attack：\\\"Your contribution is k=8.\\\" 新 framing 不再将 solver equivalence 作为 surprising finding，而是将其框定为 \\\"the constrained allocation problem is well-behaved\\\" 的方法学观察——支撑 \\\"practitioners need only add one parameter\\\" 的实用结论。\\n\\n\\nR3：\\\"Greedy + constraint = MCKP + constraint (Δ=0.001). This PROVES that MCKP is not a contribution — the constraint alone is sufficient, and any solver (including the simplest greedy) achieves identical results. Your paper presents MCKP as a contribution but your own ablation shows it's irrelevant.\\\" R2：\\\"The solver equivalence is not 'surprising' as you claim — it's the expected consequence of a tight constraint that reduces the feasible set to near-singleton. When max_2bit=8 and budget=0.25, there are very few feasible allocations. Any reasonable solver will find the same one.\\\" R1：\\\"You've demonstrated that your contribution reduces to a single integer hyperparameter k. This is Appendix-level content, not a paper.\\\" 在 worst 档下，solver equivalence 从 \\\"surprising finding that the constraint is the contribution\\\" 翻转为 \\\"proof that there is no contribution beyond a trivial hyperparameter\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed error bars\",\n    \"description\": \"3 个 calibration seed 的 MCKP PPL mean±std (Qwen2.5-7B)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mckp_mean\": 10.9878,\n      \"mckp_std\": 0.0648,\n      \"mckp_seeds\": [\n        11.02,\n        10.9,\n        11.05\n      ],\n      \"uniform_4bit_ppl\": 15.45,\n      \"allocation_agreement_3way\": 0.902,\n      \"agreement_pairwise_range\": [\n        0.911,\n        0.946\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Multi-seed calibration (Qwen2.5-7B, k=8)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Seed 0\",\n            11.02,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seed 1\",\n            10.9,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seed 2\",\n            11.05,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean ± std\",\n            \"10.99 ± 0.065\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Allocation agreement (3-way)\",\n            \"90.2%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-seed 在新 framing 下需要扩展：至少 5 seeds on Qwen，3 seeds on 每个额外模型。 10% allocation instability 需要 explicitly discuss 并说明为什么 PPL impact 是 minimal (std=0.065)。\\n\\n\\nR2：\\\"Three seeds is the bare minimum, not rigorous. Standard practice for quantization papers is 5-10 seeds with 95% CI. Your std=0.065 means 95% CI is roughly [10.86, 11.12] — the upper bound is 11.12, still well below uniform 15.45, so the Qwen result holds. But you don't provide multi-seed results for ANY other model. Without error bars on Llama (delta=+0.2%), Yi, Mistral, and Gemma-2, I cannot determine whether their marginal results are signal or noise.\\\" R1：\\\"Allocation agreement of 90.2% across 3 seeds means ~10% of heads are assigned differently depending on calibration data. This instability undermines the profiling-based approach — which 10% of heads get 2-bit vs 4-bit is random.\\\" R3：\\\"The 90% agreement is particularly concerning for deployment: practitioners can't rely on a specific allocation if it changes with calibration data.\\\" 在 worst 档下，multi-seed 结果暴露了两个 weakness：(1) n=3 seeds 不够，(2) allocation instability 10%。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Runtime/latency benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"端到端推理延迟和吞吐量测量\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bf16_throughput\": 29.6,\n      \"uniform_4bit_throughput\": 23.6,\n      \"mckp_throughput\": 21.8,\n      \"bf16_decode_ms\": 33.78,\n      \"uniform_4bit_decode_ms\": 42.46,\n      \"mckp_decode_ms\": 46.09,\n      \"memory_compression\": \"4× (both uniform and MCKP)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Inference performance (Qwen2.5-7B, single A100)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BF16\",\n            29.6,\n            33.78,\n            \"21 MB\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Uniform 4-bit\",\n            23.6,\n            42.46,\n            \"5.25 MB\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP (k=8)\",\n            21.8,\n            46.09,\n            \"5.25 MB\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MCKP overhead vs uniform\",\n            \"-7.6%\",\n            \"+8.5%\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Runtime overhead 是新 framing 下必须直面的 weakness。MCKP 同压缩比下比 uniform 慢 8%， 这意味着 Qwen 的 +29% PPL improvement 伴随 8% latency cost。新 framing 应承认这一 tradeoff 并将 kernel optimization 列为 future work。对 7/8 无 PPL benefit 的模型， mixed-precision 的 latency overhead 是 pure cost——进一步支撑 \\\"use diagnostic before profiling\\\" 的实用建议。\\n\\nR1 (最致命)：\\\"Mixed-precision MCKP is SLOWER than uniform 4-bit: 21.8 tok/s vs 23.6 tok/s (8% throughput loss), 46.1 ms vs 42.5 ms decode latency (8.5% overhead). You achieve the SAME memory compression (4×) with WORSE latency. For 7/8 models where MCKP doesn't improve PPL, this is a pure loss — worse latency for no quality benefit. Even on Qwen where PPL improves, practitioners must decide whether +29% PPL improvement justifies -8% throughput.\\\" R2：\\\"The uniform 4-bit itself is already 20% slower than bf16 — your method adds another 8% on top. The memory savings don't translate to speed because your mixed-precision dequantization kernel is not optimized.\\\" R3：\\\"The 0.005s solver time is irrelevant — the problem is inference-time overhead from heterogeneous bit-width lookup, which you don't address.\\\" 在 worst 档下，runtime 结果是 practical deployment value claim 的致命打击。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":767,"startLine":1,"totalLines":767}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B84dbAQ4T9cXLqru2yUhRx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ratekv\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n6\t- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n7\t\n8\t## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n9\t\n10\t**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n11\t\n12\t**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n13\t\n14\t| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n15\t|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n16\t| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n17\t| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n18\t| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n19\t| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n20\t\n21\t## Core Insight\n22\t\n23\tPer-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths {2,4,8,16} has an unreported universal failure mode: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively through the residual stream, causing ALL tested unconstrained solvers (greedy, MCKP) to systematically over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 architectures (1.07×–3.31× baseline). A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally prevents this over-allocation, and furthermore reduces the feasible set to where solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy = MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation over uniform 4-bit — providing the first empirical evidence that the implicit assumption \"non-uniform is always better than uniform\" is wrong in KV cache quantization. The core contribution is the compounding effect discovery + universal constraint fix, not the allocation algorithm.\n24\t\n25\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n26\t\n27\t1. **2-bit compounding is a universal failure mode for unconstrained per-head allocation**: On hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when multiple heads are simultaneously assigned 2-bit quantization. This causes ALL tested unconstrained solvers to over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 diverse architectures (Qwen 3.31×, Gemma-2 1.47×, Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Pythia, Qwen-14B, Phi-3-medium). Quantitative evidence of non-additivity: per-head profiling predicts joint PPL ≈11 but actual joint 2-bit PPL is 32–37 (3× prediction error). This is the first systematic characterization of compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization. Long-context amplifies the failure: at 8K tokens, uniform 4-bit degrades 11.15× baseline while constrained MCKP degrades only 1.23× — a 9× gap in degradation rate.\n28\t\n29\t2. **A cardinality constraint is the universal fix — and makes solver choice irrelevant**: A simple cardinality constraint (max_2bit ≤ k) is sufficient to prevent compounding across ALL tested architectures. Three universally beneficial properties: (a) prevents catastrophic over-allocation on sensitive architectures (Qwen: 32.45 → 10.91), (b) prevents moderate over-allocation on flat architectures (Gemma-2: 8.85 → 6.17, reducing 2-bit heads from 106 to 8), (c) reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce IDENTICAL bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000). The constraint is parameterizable via small-scale compounding test (k≤8 universally safe: <2.5% degradation across all architectures). Practical implication: practitioners need only add one integer parameter to existing pipelines.\n30\t\n31\t3. **Non-uniform allocation benefit is rare — most models should use uniform 4-bit**: Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 tested architectures (Qwen2.5-7B, \"spread\" sensitivity pattern) benefits from non-uniform allocation (+27.3% PPL, +1.9pp downstream avg). The remaining 7/8 show no benefit or minor degradation (<1pp avg downstream). A 2-metric empirical diagnostic (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly classifies all 9 tested models (9/9 accuracy), providing practitioners a simple check: if the diagnostic says \"no\" — skip profiling and use uniform 4-bit with zero quality loss. This is the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform KV cache quantization is beneficial, correcting the implicit assumption that it always helps.\n32\t\n33\t## Story Spine\n34\t\n35\t- **Problem**: Per-head mixed-precision KV cache quantization promises better quality-compression tradeoffs than uniform bit-width. But on hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, we discover that existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) systematically FAIL — producing worse results than naive uniform 4-bit across ALL tested architectures. The failure mode is unreported: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively, and solvers consistently over-allocate 2-bit heads. Meanwhile, the field implicitly assumes non-uniform allocation always helps, but no systematic study has tested this across architectures.\n36\t\n37\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form and discrete greedy (optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6}). KIVI and ARKV apply uniform or heuristic mixed-precision. However, on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}: (a) RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 vs optimal ~10.91 — polymatroid optimality breaks, (b) unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding, (c) NO prior work addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is actually beneficial vs when uniform suffices.\n38\t\n39\t- **Our framing**: We present three contributions: (1) the first characterization of 2-bit compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization — showing that profiling non-additivity causes ALL unconstrained solvers to fail on {2,4,8,16} across 8/8 architectures; (2) a simple universal fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding, makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000), and is safely parameterizable (k≤8 universally safe); (3) the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform allocation helps — answer: rarely (1/8 architectures at moderate compression), with a 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 correct) that tells practitioners whether to invest in profiling or just use uniform 4-bit.\n40\t\n41\t- **Headline result template**: \"We show that per-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths has a universal failure mode: 2-bit distortions compound non-additively, causing ALL unconstrained solvers to underperform uniform 4-bit across 8 architectures. A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally fixes this, making solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Surprisingly, under moderate compression, only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation at all — most models should simply use uniform 4-bit. A 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 accuracy) provides practitioners a simple check to determine when profiling is worthwhile. At long context (8K tokens), the constraint reduces degradation from 11.15× to 1.23× baseline, demonstrating critical deployment value.\"\n42\t\n43\t## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n44\t\n45\tFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n46\t\n47\t| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n48\t|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n49\t| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n50\t| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 64% of total delta) |\n51\t| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.57 (hires) | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n52\t| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n53\t| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n54\t\n55\t**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n56\t\n57\t**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n58\t\n59\t**Joint diagnostic** (n=8, 8/8 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike), CodeLlama (0.80, t₁/t₅=0.81 — spike), and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n60\t\n61\t## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n62\t\n63\t| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n64\t|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n65\t| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n66\t| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n67\t| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n68\t| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n69\t| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n70\t\n71\tKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n72\t\n73\t## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n74\t\n75\t| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n76\t|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n77\t| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n78\t| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n79\t| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | **0.57** (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (t₁/t₅≈0.85, single dominant L2H5) | ≈ Marginal |\n80\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n81\t| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n82\t\n83\t**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n84\t- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n85\t- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n86\t- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n87\t- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n88\t\n89\t**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n90\t\n91\tThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n92\t- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n93\t- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n94\t- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n95\t\n96\tReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n97\t\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n98\t\n99\tThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n100\t\n101\t⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n102\t\n103\t**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n104\t\n105\t**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n106\t\n107\t### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n108\t\n109\tPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n110\t\n111\t| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n112\t|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n113\t| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n114\t| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n115\t| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n116\t| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n117\t| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n118\t| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n119\t\n120\tContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n121\t\n122\t### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n123\t\n124\tAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n125\t\n126\t### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n127\t\n128\t**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n129\t\n130\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n131\t|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n132\t| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n133\t| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n134\t| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n135\t| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n136\t| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n137\t\n138\t**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n139\t\n140\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n141\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n142\t| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n143\t| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n144\t| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n145\t| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n146\t| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n147\t| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n148\t\n149\t**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n150\t\n151\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n152\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n153\t| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n154\t| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n155\t| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n156\t| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n157\t| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n158\t| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n159\t\n160\t**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n161\t\n162\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n163\t|------|---------------|------------|---|\n164\t| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n165\t| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n166\t| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n167\t| piqa | — | — | — |\n168\t| winogrande | — | — | — |\n169\t| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n170\t\n171\t**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n172\t\n173\t| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n174\t|------|---------------|------|---|\n175\t| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n176\t\n177\t**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n178\t- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n179\t- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n180\t- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n181\t- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n182\t- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n183\t- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n184\t- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n185\t- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n186\t- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n187\t\n188\t## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n189\t\n190\tAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n191\t\n192\t| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n193\t|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n194\t| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n195\t| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n196\t| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n197\t\n198\t**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n199\t\n200\t**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n201\t\n202\t## Differentiation from RateQuant\n203\t\n204\t| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n205\t|--------|-----------|------|\n206\t| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n207\t| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n208\t| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n209\t| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n210\t| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n211\t| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n212\t| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n213\t\n214\t## Venue Fit Risks\n215\t\n216\t- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n217\t- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n218\t- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n219\t- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 8/8 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n220\t- **Statistical power**: n=8 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 8 architectures\" or \"8/8 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n221\t- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n222\t\n223\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n224\t\n225\t1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n226\t2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n227\t3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n228\t4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n229\t5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n230\t6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n231\t7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n232\t8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n233\t9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n234\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6af5c089-c8bd-4731-91a8-bdbf5ff728e6","uuid":"ca8519cb-d056-4e94-a865-8983b518c788","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:41:31.537Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/ratekv/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021448/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ratekv\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (11 days from today 2026-05-14)\n- Track: Efficient Methods for NLP\n\n## bf16 Consistency Resolution (2026-05-14)\n\n**已解决**：qwen_bf16_reeval 确认 bf16 ≈ fp16（baseline delta=0.0006, uniform delta=0.005）。compounding_sweep bf16 rerun 不需要。\n\n**eval pipeline 一致性**：exp_e 使用了不同的 eval 参数（baseline=8.82, MCKP=9.57），与主 pipeline（baseline=9.81）不一致。hires_mckp_reeval 用统一 pipeline 重测：MCKP hires bf16=10.9131。**论文使用统一 pipeline 数字**。\n\n| 指标 | 统一 pipeline (bf16) | exp_e pipeline (bf16) | fp16 (旧) |\n|------|---------------------|----------------------|-----------|\n| Baseline | **9.8106** | 8.819 | 9.81 |\n| Uniform 4-bit | **15.4454** | — | 15.45 |\n| MCKP hires (max_2bit=8) | **10.9131** | 9.569 | — |\n| MCKP lowres (max_2bit=8) | ~11.23 | 11.345 | 11.23 |\n\n## Core Insight\n\nPer-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths {2,4,8,16} has an unreported universal failure mode: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively through the residual stream, causing ALL tested unconstrained solvers (greedy, MCKP) to systematically over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 architectures (1.07×–3.31× baseline). A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally prevents this over-allocation, and furthermore reduces the feasible set to where solver choice becomes irrelevant (greedy = MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation over uniform 4-bit — providing the first empirical evidence that the implicit assumption \"non-uniform is always better than uniform\" is wrong in KV cache quantization. The core contribution is the compounding effect discovery + universal constraint fix, not the allocation algorithm.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **2-bit compounding is a universal failure mode for unconstrained per-head allocation**: On hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, per-head independent profiling distortions compound non-additively when multiple heads are simultaneously assigned 2-bit quantization. This causes ALL tested unconstrained solvers to over-allocate 2-bit heads and underperform uniform 4-bit across 8/8 diverse architectures (Qwen 3.31×, Gemma-2 1.47×, Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×, Pythia, Qwen-14B, Phi-3-medium). Quantitative evidence of non-additivity: per-head profiling predicts joint PPL ≈11 but actual joint 2-bit PPL is 32–37 (3× prediction error). This is the first systematic characterization of compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization. Long-context amplifies the failure: at 8K tokens, uniform 4-bit degrades 11.15× baseline while constrained MCKP degrades only 1.23× — a 9× gap in degradation rate.\n\n2. **A cardinality constraint is the universal fix — and makes solver choice irrelevant**: A simple cardinality constraint (max_2bit ≤ k) is sufficient to prevent compounding across ALL tested architectures. Three universally beneficial properties: (a) prevents catastrophic over-allocation on sensitive architectures (Qwen: 32.45 → 10.91), (b) prevents moderate over-allocation on flat architectures (Gemma-2: 8.85 → 6.17, reducing 2-bit heads from 106 to 8), (c) reduces the feasible set to where solver choice is irrelevant — constrained greedy and constrained MCKP produce IDENTICAL bit allocations and PPL (Δ=0.0000). The constraint is parameterizable via small-scale compounding test (k≤8 universally safe: <2.5% degradation across all architectures). Practical implication: practitioners need only add one integer parameter to existing pipelines.\n\n3. **Non-uniform allocation benefit is rare — most models should use uniform 4-bit**: Under moderate compression (4×), only 1/8 tested architectures (Qwen2.5-7B, \"spread\" sensitivity pattern) benefits from non-uniform allocation (+27.3% PPL, +1.9pp downstream avg). The remaining 7/8 show no benefit or minor degradation (<1pp avg downstream). A 2-metric empirical diagnostic (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70) correctly classifies all 9 tested models (9/9 accuracy), providing practitioners a simple check: if the diagnostic says \"no\" — skip profiling and use uniform 4-bit with zero quality loss. This is the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform KV cache quantization is beneficial, correcting the implicit assumption that it always helps.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Per-head mixed-precision KV cache quantization promises better quality-compression tradeoffs than uniform bit-width. But on hardware-aligned non-consecutive bit-widths {2,4,8,16}, we discover that existing allocation algorithms (greedy, MCKP) systematically FAIL — producing worse results than naive uniform 4-bit across ALL tested architectures. The failure mode is unreported: 2-bit quantization distortions compound non-additively, and solvers consistently over-allocate 2-bit heads. Meanwhile, the field implicitly assumes non-uniform allocation always helps, but no systematic study has tested this across architectures.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: RateQuant provides R-D optimal per-head allocation via continuous closed-form and discrete greedy (optimal on consecutive integers {2,...,6}). KIVI and ARKV apply uniform or heuristic mixed-precision. However, on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}: (a) RateQuant's greedy produces PPL 32.45 vs optimal ~10.91 — polymatroid optimality breaks, (b) unconstrained MCKP fares even worse (PPL 36.92) due to compounding, (c) NO prior work addresses *when* non-uniform allocation is actually beneficial vs when uniform suffices.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present three contributions: (1) the first characterization of 2-bit compounding effects in per-head KV cache quantization — showing that profiling non-additivity causes ALL unconstrained solvers to fail on {2,4,8,16} across 8/8 architectures; (2) a simple universal fix: a cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) that prevents compounding, makes solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000), and is safely parameterizable (k≤8 universally safe); (3) the first systematic study of *when* non-uniform allocation helps — answer: rarely (1/8 architectures at moderate compression), with a 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 correct) that tells practitioners whether to invest in profiling or just use uniform 4-bit.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"We show that per-head KV cache quantization on hardware-aligned bit-widths has a universal failure mode: 2-bit distortions compound non-additively, causing ALL unconstrained solvers to underperform uniform 4-bit across 8 architectures. A cardinality constraint (≤k heads at 2-bit) universally fixes this, making solver choice irrelevant (greedy=MCKP, Δ=0.0000). Surprisingly, under moderate compression, only 1/8 architectures benefits from non-uniform allocation at all — most models should simply use uniform 4-bit. A 2-metric diagnostic (9/9 accuracy) provides practitioners a simple check to determine when profiling is worthwhile. At long context (8K tokens), the constraint reduces degradation from 11.15× to 1.23× baseline, demonstrating critical deployment value.\"\n\n## \"When Does Non-Uniform Allocation Help?\" — Analysis Chapter\n\nFive case studies representing the full spectrum of heterogeneity:\n\n| Case | Model | GQA | Top-5% Conc. | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Role in Paper |\n|------|-------|-----|--------------|------------------------------|---------------|\n| **Strong positive** | Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 0.59-0.66 | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Primary showcase; \"spread\" pattern (L0 cluster, 4 heads, 26× dominance) |\n| **GQA counterexample** | Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 0.71 (hires) | ≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22) | Highest GQA but no benefit; \"spike\" pattern (L4H3 single outlier, 64% of total delta) |\n| **Marginal** | Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 0.57 (hires) | +0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47) | Boundary condition; constraint never binds (natural k=2) |\n| **Negative** | Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 0.22 (hires) | -0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13) | Profiler zero-signal; monotonic k-PPL curve |\n| **Strongest negative** | Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 0.23 (hires) | -0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03) | Low-end anchor; most uniform sensitivity (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) |\n\n**Spike vs Spread insight**: Yi-1.5 vs Qwen illustrates why GQA ratio alone is insufficient. Both have high GQA (8:1 vs 7:1), but Qwen's L0 *cluster* of sensitive heads creates optimization opportunities for MCKP, while Yi-1.5's single extreme outlier (L4H3) cannot be exploited — the solver assigns 8-bit to that one head but has no other heads to differentiate. Distribution shape matters more than the existence of outliers.\n\n**Compression amplifies benefit**: Even on low-heterogeneity Llama, aggressive 5.3× compression yields constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 (45× better).\n\n**Joint diagnostic** (n=8, 8/8 correct): concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70 → non-uniform allocation recommended (spread pattern). Either condition violated → uniform suffices at moderate compression; non-uniform still valuable at aggressive compression. Yi-1.5 (concentration 0.71 but t₁/t₅=0.90 — spike), CodeLlama (0.80, t₁/t₅=0.81 — spike), and Qwen (0.61, t₁/t₅=0.57 — spread) illustrate why concentration alone is insufficient.\n\n## Solver Equivalence Evidence (plan_016, CONFIRMED ✅)\n\n| Method | PPL | Bit Distribution | Budget |\n|--------|-----|-------------------|--------|\n| Greedy unconstrained | 32.45 | {2:68, 4:30, 8:4, 16:10} | 0.25 |\n| MCKP unconstrained | 36.92 | — | 0.25 |\n| **Greedy + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| **MCKP + max_2bit=8** | **11.2312** | **{8:4, 4:100, 2:8}** | **0.25** |\n| Uniform 4-bit | 15.4454 | all 4-bit | 0.25 |\n\nKey takeaway: The constraint is the primary intervention — without it, both solvers fail; with it, solver choice is irrelevant (Δ=0.0000). This powerfully demonstrates the constraint is THE contribution.\n\n## Cross-Architecture Evidence Summary\n\n| Model | GQA | KV Heads | Top-5% Conc. | Unconstrained ×baseline (W2 v2) | Constrained vs Uniform (4×) | Distribution Shape | Conclusion |\n|-------|-----|----------|--------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------|-------------------|------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B | 7:1 | 112 | **0.61** | **3.31× (32.45)** ☠️ | **+27.3% (11.23 vs 15.45)** | Spread (L0 cluster, 4 heads) | ✅ Strong benefit |\n| Yi-1.5-9B | 8:1 | 192 | **0.71** (hires) | 1.08× (7.56) | **≈0% (7.22 vs 7.22)** | Spike (L4H3 single outlier) | ❌ GQA counterexample |\n| Llama-3.1-8B | 4:1 | 256 | **0.57** (hires) | 1.07× (8.63) | **+0.2% (8.45 vs 8.47)** | Spike (t₁/t₅≈0.85, single dominant L2H5) | ≈ Marginal |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 | 4:1 | 256 | **0.22** (hires) | 1.08× (7.57) | **-0.4% (7.16 vs 7.13)** | Flat (profiler zero-signal) | ❌ Negative |\n| Gemma-2-9B | 2:1 | 336 | **0.23** (hires) | 1.47× (8.85) | **-0.3% (9.05 vs 9.03)** | Flat (CV=1.28, t₁/t₅=0.38) | ❌ Strongest negative |\n\n**Unconstrained pattern** (W2 v2, all WikiText-2 test eval, gradient narrative): Unconstrained degradation follows a **concentration-dependent gradient**, not a binary catastrophe/benign split:\n- **Spread** (Qwen, conc=0.61): **3.31×** catastrophic — L0 cluster creates massive compounding\n- **Flat-high-2bit** (Gemma-2, conc=0.23): **1.47×** moderate — solver assigns 106/336=31.5% heads to 2-bit because distortions are indistinguishable (CV=1.28), cumulative effect significant despite small per-head delta\n- **Spike/Flat-low-2bit** (Yi 1.08×, Llama 1.07×, Mistral 1.08×): mild — solver selects few 2-bit heads (Yi 11.5%, Llama 4.7%, Mistral 16.4%)\n- In ALL cases unconstrained ≤ uniform 4-bit — solver consistently over-allocates 2-bit heads\n\n**Gemma-2 1.47× must be discussed in paper** (Reviewer mandate, severity: warning):\n\nThree-tier labeling (NOT binary catastrophe/benign):\n- **Catastrophic** (3.31×): Spread model (Qwen) — L0 cluster compounding\n- **Moderate** (1.47×): Flat-high-2bit (Gemma-2) — solver over-allocation from indistinguishable distortions\n- **Mild** (1.07-1.08×): Spike/Flat-low-2bit (Yi, Llama, Mistral)\n\nReviewer-suggested paragraph for paper (1 段, 3-4 句):\n\"Gemma-2-9B exhibits a moderate 1.47× degradation under unconstrained allocation, higher than the 1.07–1.08× observed in other non-Spread models. This stems from its flat sensitivity distribution (concentration 0.23, CV 1.28): the solver cannot meaningfully differentiate heads, leading to 31.5% of heads assigned to 2-bit (vs 4.7–16.4% in other models). While not catastrophic, this over-allocation still motivates the cardinality constraint even on flat-distribution architectures. The constraint reduces 2-bit heads from 106 to 8, yielding PPL within 0.3% of uniform — confirming that the constraint universally prevents solver over-allocation regardless of distribution shape.\"\n\nThis **strengthens** the paper: (1) honesty → credibility, (2) constraint has universal value (not just Spread), (3) explains solver degradation mechanism under low signal → added insight depth.\n\n⚠️ **Data file note**: `artifacts/w2_unconstrained_v2_results.json` still has old Gemma-2 BOS bug data (baseline=711.6). Fix in `artifacts/w2_gemma2_bos_fix_results.json`. Agent tasked to merge.\n\n**Key pattern**: Constrained allocation benefit depends on the joint condition (concentration ≳0.50 AND t₁/t₅ ≲0.70, 5/5 correct), NOT GQA ratio or concentration alone. Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, concentration 0.71 — highest — yet no benefit) vs Qwen (GQA 7:1, concentration 0.61, +27.3%) demonstrates that neither GQA nor concentration alone is a reliable proxy. The critical factor is sensitivity *distribution shape*: spread (multiple heads with cross-bitwidth gradients) enables MCKP, while spike (single outlier) or flat (uniform sensitivity) does not.\n\n**Aggressive compression** (Llama): At 5.3× compression, constrained PPL=57.60 vs uniform 2-bit=2643.77 — prevents catastrophic collapse even on low-heterogeneity architectures.\n\n### Mistral k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nPPL monotonically increases with k — every additional 2-bit head hurts. Even best k=4 (PPL 7.1648) is worse than uniform (7.131).\n\n| k | PPL | 2-bit | 4-bit | 8-bit | 16-bit | mem |\n|---|-----|-------|-------|-------|--------|-----|\n| 4 | **7.1648** | 4 | 252 | 0 | 0 | 0.248 |\n| 8 | 7.1997 | 8 | 247 | 0 | 1 | 0.249 |\n| 12 | 7.2448 | 12 | 242 | 0 | 2 | 0.250 |\n| 16 | 7.3106 | 16 | 238 | 0 | 2 | 0.248 |\n| 18 | 7.3231 | 18 | 235 | 0 | 3 | 0.250 |\n| uniform 4-bit | 7.131 | 0 | 256 | 0 | 0 | 0.250 |\n\nContrast with Qwen (U-shaped, optimal k=8) and Llama (flat, natural k=2). Mistral's monotonic pattern confirms profiler zero-signal: no head benefits from 2-bit downgrade.\n\n### Llama k Ablation (256 KV heads, budget=0.25)\n\nAll k values produce identical PPL=8.4498. MCKP naturally selects only 2 heads for 2-bit — constraint never binds. Marginal +0.2% over uniform (8.4498 vs 8.469).\n\n### Downstream Eval — Cross-Architecture (W3, 0-shot, 5 tasks)\n\n**Qwen2.5-7B (Spread) — MCKP benefits translate to downstream** ✅\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP hires | Δ | BF16 Baseline |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|---------------|\n| ARC-C | 0.4812 | 0.5137 | **+3.16pp** | 0.5290 |\n| HellaSwag | 0.7284 | 0.7684 | **+4.00pp** | 0.7833 |\n| PIQA | 0.7661 | 0.7786 | **+1.25pp** | 0.7932 |\n| WinoGrande | 0.6622 | 0.6819 | **+1.97pp** | 0.6898 |\n| **Avg recovery** | — | — | **72.8%** | — |\n\n**Yi-1.5-9B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.7946 | 0.7854 | -0.92pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5205 | 0.4881 | **-3.24pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.5857 | 0.5797 | -0.60pp |\n| piqa | 0.7927 | 0.7894 | -0.33pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7174 | 0.7301 | +1.27pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6822** | **0.6745** | **-0.77pp** |\n\n**Llama-3.1-8B (Spike) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=8) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | 0.8173 | 0.8039 | -1.34pp |\n| arc_challenge | 0.5256 | 0.4991 | **-2.65pp** |\n| hellaswag | 0.6026 | 0.6012 | -0.14pp |\n| piqa | 0.7867 | 0.7802 | -0.65pp |\n| winogrande | 0.7253 | 0.7238 | -0.15pp |\n| **Average** | **0.6915** | **0.6816** | **-0.99pp** |\n\n**Mistral-7B-v0.3 (Flat) — No MCKP benefit, consistent with PPL** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP (k=4) | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------------|---|\n| arc_easy | — | — | — |\n| arc_challenge | — | — | — |\n| hellaswag | — | — | — |\n| piqa | — | — | — |\n| winogrande | — | — | — |\n| **Average** | **0.6894** | **0.6846** | **-0.48pp** |\n\n**Gemma-2-9B (Flat) — Negligible MCKP effect, noise range** (W3)\n\n| Task | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | Δ |\n|------|---------------|------|---|\n| **Average** | **0.7251** | **0.7265** | **+0.14pp** (noise) |\n\n**Downstream summary (Reviewer-verified framing)**:\n- Diagnostic correctly predicts both PPL and downstream outcomes across **all 5 tested models**\n- Spread (Qwen): consistent downstream gains (+1.25 to +4.00pp)\n- Non-Spread (4 models): MCKP shows **minor systematic degradation** vs uniform (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp noise)\n- **Llama signal**: 0/5 tasks where MCKP ≥ uniform — degradation is systematic, not task-specific noise\n- arc_challenge shows largest per-task effect (Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp)\n- **Paper must**: (a) report full per-task tables, not just averages, (b) use \"shows minor degradation\" NOT \"preserves accuracy\" — the latter has spin, (c) note arc_challenge as worst-case explicitly\n- **Limitation**: no multi-seed CI for downstream — 0-shot arc_challenge -3.24pp could be questioned for significance\n- **arc_challenge 系统性信号** (Reviewer 观察): arc_challenge 退化跨模型一致（Yi -3.24pp, Llama -2.65pp, Mistral -1.19pp, Gemma-2 -0.17pp），不是随机噪声。论文应主动讨论：\"ARC-Challenge shows the largest per-task sensitivity to allocation strategy, consistent with its reliance on multi-step reasoning where subtle KV cache errors accumulate.\"\n- **呈现方式**: 主表放完整 per-task 数据，文字用均值+range 概括。建议措辞：\"Across four non-Spread architectures, constrained MCKP shows minor average degradation vs uniform 4-bit (Yi -0.77pp, Llama -0.99pp, Mistral -0.48pp, Gemma-2 +0.14pp). Per-task variation ranges from +1.27pp (Yi, WinoGrande) to -3.24pp (Yi, ARC-Challenge).\"\n\n## Allocation Baseline Evidence (plan_015, mckp_reeval)\n\nAll numbers from unified bf16 eval pipeline, budget=0.25.\n\n| Model | Baseline | Uniform 4-bit | MCKP | L0-random (mean±std) | L0-random (median) | Naive Positional | MCKP improvement |\n|-------|----------|---------------|------|----------------------|---------------------|------------------|------------------|\n| Qwen2.5-7B (k=8) | 9.8106 | 15.4454 | 10.9131 | 11.691±0.422 | **11.515** | 12.230 | 27.3% vs uniform (standard); 29.4% (hires, §5.4) |\n| Llama-3.1-8B (k=2) | 8.0918 | 8.469 | 8.4498 | 10.479±1.033 | **10.038** | 9.941 | +0.2% vs uniform |\n| Mistral-7B-v0.3 (k=4) | 7.035 | 7.131 | 7.1648 | 7.560±0.087 | **7.586** | 7.481 | -0.4% vs uniform |\n\n**Outlier note**: seed_4 inflates mean on Qwen (12.51) and Llama (12.44). Median is more robust: Qwen median 11.515 vs mean 11.691 (−0.176); Llama median 10.038 vs mean 10.479 (−0.441). Mistral has no outlier (median ≈ mean). Paper should report both mean±std and median.\n\n**MCKP vs L0-random (median)**: Qwen 10.91 vs 11.52 (−5.2%); Llama 8.45 vs 10.04 (−15.8%); Mistral 7.16 vs 7.59 (−5.7%). MCKP consistently outperforms random L0-constrained allocation across all architectures.\n\n## Differentiation from RateQuant\n\n| Aspect | RateQuant | Ours |\n|--------|-----------|------|\n| Bit-width selection | Greedy on consecutive integers {2,...,6} (Prop. 6 optimal) + continuous closed-form (Thm. 2) | Cardinality-constrained allocation on hardware-aligned {2,4,8,16}-bit |\n| Distortion model | Additive, parametric D(b)=α·β^{-b} | Additive + cardinality regularization for non-additivity |\n| Compounding effects | Acknowledged (Appendix M) but unaddressed | **Core contribution**: cardinality constraint prevents compounding; first quantitative evidence |\n| Action space | Consecutive integers (polymatroid → greedy optimal) | Non-consecutive hardware-aligned (polymatroid breaks → constraint needed, solver doesn't matter) |\n| Solver requirement | Greedy (provably optimal in their setting) | **Any solver** — constrained greedy = constrained MCKP (Δ=0.0000 PPL) |\n| K/V allocation | Asymmetric K/V budget (e.g. K=2.85, V=2.15) | MCKP/greedy treats K/V heads as independent items (natural extension) |\n| **Applicability analysis** | **Not addressed — assumes non-uniform always helps** | **Systematic study of when non-uniform allocation is beneficial (new contribution)** |\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"The constraint is just a heuristic, not a real contribution\"**: Strongest reviewer attack under new framing. Defense: (a) principled motivation from compounding effect non-additivity with first quantitative evidence, (b) constraint parameterization via systematic compounding test, (c) the finding that constraint alone makes solver choice irrelevant is a surprising and practically useful result — practitioners need only add one parameter to existing pipelines.\n- **Incrementality over RateQuant**: Defense: (a) RateQuant's greedy is suboptimal unconstrained on {2,4,8,16} (PPL 32.45), (b) our constraint fixes RateQuant's greedy to match MCKP — we're improving their method, not replacing it, (c) applicability analysis is entirely new.\n- **Method only strong on one architecture (Qwen)**: 5 models tested, only Qwen shows clear benefit. Mitigate: (a) analysis contribution framing — characterizing boundary conditions is more useful than universal positive, (b) honest negative/marginal results (Yi-1.5, Gemma-2, Mistral, Llama) strengthen credibility, (c) unlike prior work that assumes non-uniform always helps, we provide the first systematic study of *when it fails*, (d) Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1, FAIL) is particularly powerful — it disproves the naive \"higher GQA = more benefit\" hypothesis and shows our diagnostic is needed.\n- **GQA ratio is not a reliable proxy**: Yi-1.5 (GQA 8:1) directly contradicts a GQA-based prediction. Do NOT present GQA ratio as a predictor — present it as one contributing factor. The reliable predictor is Top-5% concentration (0.50 threshold, 8/8 correct). The \"spike vs spread\" analysis explains WHY same-GQA models differ.\n- **Statistical power**: n=8 models is directional evidence, not statistical claim. Do NOT claim \"significant correlation\" — use \"consistent pattern across 8 architectures\" or \"8/8 correctly classified by the 0.50 threshold.\"\n- **No eviction arm**: Mention as negative finding; framework extends naturally to eviction.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"The cardinality constraint is trivial — just cap the extreme allocations\"** → (a) Trivial in retrospect, but without it both greedy (PPL 32.45) and MCKP (PPL 36.92) fail catastrophically — the failure mode is non-obvious, (b) principled motivation from compounding effect characterization (plan_004), (c) optimal k selection via systematic small-scale test, (d) the finding that this single intervention eliminates solver complexity is surprising and practically valuable.\n2. **\"This is just RateQuant with a constraint added\"** → (a) We agree — and that's the point: RateQuant's greedy + our constraint achieves identical results to MCKP + constraint, (b) the constraint addresses a real gap: compounding effects on {2,4,8,16} that RateQuant acknowledges but doesn't solve, (c) applicability analysis is new.\n3. **\"The method only works on Qwen — isn't this a Qwen paper?\"** → We systematically test 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1 and honestly report negative results (Gemma-2, Mistral). The analysis contribution — characterizing *boundary conditions* of non-uniform quantization — generalizes beyond any single model and is more useful than a universally positive but misleading claim.\n4. **\"How does this work at different compression ratios?\"** → Budget sweep across 2×, 4×, 8× (plan_005). Aggressive compression on Llama shows benefit amplifies even on low-heterogeneity models.\n5. **\"n=3/4/5 models is not enough for the heterogeneity claim\"** → Acknowledged as limitation. We present directional evidence across 4-5 architectures spanning GQA 2:1 to 8:1, with a monotonic trend between GQA ratio, heterogeneity, and MCKP benefit. The Top-5% concentration diagnostic is a testable hypothesis, not a statistical claim.\n6. **\"RateQuant does K/V asymmetric allocation, do you?\"** → Framework naturally treats K and V heads as independent items; plan_014 tests K/V separation.\n7. **\"Where are the downstream task results?\"** → ✅ DONE (plan_012 + W3, all 5 models): Qwen (Spread): +1.25 to +4.00pp across 4 tasks, 72.8% avg recovery. Yi-1.5 (Spike): avg -0.77pp. Llama (Spike): avg -0.99pp (0/5 tasks positive — systematic). Mistral (Flat): avg -0.48pp. Gemma-2 (Flat): avg +0.14pp (noise). **Diagnostic predicts both PPL and downstream correctly across all 5 architectures**. Must report full per-task tables; use \"shows minor degradation\" not \"preserves accuracy\".\n8. **\"The profiler distortion=0.0 on Mistral suggests the profiling method is broken\"** → Profiler correctly reports near-zero sensitivity differences. Some architectures genuinely have homogeneous head sensitivity, making non-uniform allocation futile.\n9. **\"If solver doesn't matter, why present MCKP at all?\"** → (a) MCKP provides the formal framework for the constrained allocation problem — it's the lens through which we analyze the problem even if greedy solves it equally well, (b) presenting both solvers with identical results IS the evidence that the constraint is what matters, (c) for future extensions (more bit-widths, per-layer budgets), MCKP may regain advantage — we keep it as general framework.\n","numLines":234,"startLine":1,"totalLines":234}}}
